  "prayerPaterNosterTitle": "Pater Noster (Our Father)",
  "prayerPaterNosterContent": "Our Father, Who art in heaven, hallowed be Thy name; Thy kingdom come; Thy will be done on earth as it is in heaven. Give us this day our daily bread; and forgive us our trespasses as we forgive those who trespass against us; and lead us not into temptation, but deliver us from evil. Amen.",
  "prayerPaterNosterContentLatin": "Pater noster, qui es in caelis, sanctificetur nomen tuum. Adveniat regnum tuum. Fiat voluntas tua, sicut in caelo et in terra. Panem nostrum quotidianum da nobis hodie, et dimitte nobis debita nostra sicut et nos dimittimus debitoribus nostris. Et ne nos inducas in tentationem, sed libera nos a malo. Amen.",
  "prayerAnimaChristiTitle": "Anima Christi",
  "prayerAnimaChristiContent": "Soul of Christ, sanctify me.\nBody of Christ, save me.\nBlood of Christ, inebriate me.\nWater from the side of Christ, wash me.\nPassion of Christ, strengthen me.\nO good Jesus, hear me.\nWithin Thy wounds hide me.\nSuffer me not to be separated from Thee.\nFrom the malignant enemy defend me.\nIn the hour of my death call me\nAnd bid me come unto Thee,\nThat with Thy Saints I may praise Thee\nForever and ever. Amen.",
  "prayerAnimaChristiContentLatin": "Anima Christi, sanctifica me.\nCorpus Christi, salva me.\nSanguis Christi, inebria me.\nAqua lateris Christi, lava me.\nPassio Christi, conforta me.\nO bone Iesu, exaudi me.\nIntra tua vulnera absconde me.\nNe permittas me separari a te.\nAb hoste maligno defende me.\nIn hora mortis meae voca me.\nEt iube me venire ad te,\nUt cum Sanctis tuis laudem te,\nIn saecula saeculorum. Amen.",
  "prayerSpiritualCommunionTitle": "Spiritualis Communio",
  "prayerSpiritualCommunionContent": "My Jesus, I believe that You are present in the Most Holy Sacrament.\nI love You above all things, and I desire to receive You into my soul.\nSince I cannot at this moment receive You sacramentally, come at least spiritually into my heart.\nI embrace You as if You were already there and unite myself wholly to You. Never permit me to be separated from You. Amen.",
  "prayerSpiritualCommunionContentLatin": "Credo, mi Iesu, te in Sanctissimo Sacramento praesentem esse.\nAmo te super omnia et desidero te in anima mea recipere.\nCum iam non possim te sacramentaliter sumere, veni saltem spiritualiter in cor meum.\nEt, tamquam iam veneris, unio me totum tibi; ne permitte me unquam a te separari. Amen.",
  "prayerSelfOfferingTitle": "Suscipe (Offering of Self)",
  "prayerSelfOfferingContent": "Take, Lord, and receive all my liberty, my memory, my understanding, and my entire will, All I have and call my own. You have given all to me. To you, Lord, I return it. Everything is yours; do with it what you will. Give me only your love and your grace, that is enough for me. Amen.",
  "prayerSelfOfferingContentLatin": "Suscipe, Domine, universam meam libertatem. Accipe memoriam, intellectum, atque voluntatem omnem. Quidquid habeo vel possideo mihi largitus es; id tibi totum restituo, ac tuae prorsus voluntati trado gubernandum. Amorem tui solum cum gratia tua mihi dones, et dives sum satis, nec aliud quidquam ultra posco. Amen.",
  "prayerAveMariaTitle": "Ave Maria",
  "prayerAveMariaContent": "Hail Mary, full of grace, the Lord is with thee; blessed art thou among women, and blessed is the fruit of thy womb, Jesus. Holy Mary, Mother of God, pray for us sinners, now and at the hour of our death. Amen.",
  "prayerAveMariaContentLatin": "Ave Maria, gratia plena, Dominus tecum. Benedicta tu in mulieribus, et benedictus fructus ventris tui, Iesus. Sancta Maria, Mater Dei, ora pro nobis peccatoribus, nunc, et in hora mortis nostrae. Amen.",
  "prayerCredoTitle": "Symbolum Apostolorum (Creed)",
  "prayerCredoContent": "I believe in God, the Father Almighty, Creator of heaven and earth; and in Jesus Christ, His only Son, our Lord; who was conceived by the Holy Spirit, born of the Virgin Mary, suffered under Pontius Pilate, was crucified, died and was buried; He descended into hell; on the third day He rose again from the dead; He ascended into heaven, and sits at the right hand of God the Father Almighty; from thence He shall come to judge the living and the dead. I believe in the Holy Spirit, the holy Catholic Church, the communion of saints, the forgiveness of sins, the resurrection of the body, and life everlasting. Amen.",
  "prayerCredoContentLatin": "Credo in Deum Patrem omnipotentem, Creatorem caeli et terrae. Et in Iesum Christum, Filium eius unicum, Dominum nostrum, qui conceptus est de Spiritu Sancto, natus ex Maria Virgine, passus sub Pontio Pilato, crucifixus, mortuus, et sepultus, descendit ad inferos, tertia die resurrexit a mortuis, ascendit ad caelos, sedet ad dexteram Dei Patris omnipotentis, inde venturus est iudicare vivos et mortuos. Credo in Spiritum Sanctum, sanctam Ecclesiam catholicam, sanctorum communionem, remissionem peccatorum, carnis resurrectionem, vitam aeternam. Amen.",
  "prayerVeniCreatorTitle": "Veni Sancte Spiritus",
  "prayerVeniCreatorContent": "Come, Holy Spirit, fill the hearts of Thy faithful and enkindle in them the fire of Thy love. Send forth Thy Spirit and they shall be created. And Thou shalt renew the face of the earth.\n\nLet us pray: O God, Who didst instruct the hearts of Thy faithful by the light of the Holy Spirit, grant us in the same Spirit to be truly wise and ever to rejoice in His consolation. Through Christ our Lord. Amen.",
  "prayerVeniCreatorContentLatin": "Veni, Sancte Spiritus, reple tuorum corda fidelium, et tui amoris in eis ignem accende. Emitte Spiritum tuum et creabuntur. Et renovabis faciem terrae.\n\nOremus: Deus, qui corda fidelium Sancti Spiritus illustratione docuisti: da nobis in eodem Spiritu recta sapere, et de eius semper consolatione gaudere. Per Christum Dominum nostrum. Amen.",
  "prayerBeforeWorkTitle": "Before Work",
  "prayerBeforeWorkContent": "I offer You, O my God, the work I am about to begin; deign to bless it. I offer You my will, my intelligence, my memory, my imagination, and my body. Accept, Lord, my thoughts, my words, and my works. All that I do, I wish it to be for Your love and for Your glory. Help me, Lord, to fulfill my duty with perfection and joy. Amen.",
  "prayerMorningTitle": "Morning Prayer",
  "prayerMorningContent": "Our Father...\n\nHail Mary...\n\nCreed...\n\nMorning Offering:\nI adore You, my God, and I love You with all my heart. I thank You for having created me, made me a Christian, and preserved me this night. I offer You all the actions of this day; make them all according to Your will and for Your greater glory. Preserve me from sin and from all evil. May Your grace be always with me and with all who are dear to me.\n\nReceive, O Lord, my entire liberty. Receive my memory, my understanding, and all my will. All that I have or possess, You have given me; I give it all back to You and surrender it without reserve, so that Your will may govern all. Give me only Your love and Your grace, and I ask for nothing more, for I shall be rich enough.\n\nConsecration to Our Lady:\nO my Lady and my Mother, I offer myself entirely to you, and as a proof of my devotion, I consecrate to you this day my eyes, my ears, my mouth, my heart, and my whole being. And since I am yours, O incomparable Mother, guard me and defend me as your own possession. Amen.",
  "prayerNightTitle": "Night Prayer",
  "prayerNightContent": "Our Father... \n\nHail Mary... \n\nCreed... \n\nThanksgiving: \nI adore You, my God, and I love You with all my heart. I thank You for having created me, made me a Christian, and preserved me this day. Forgive me the faults I have committed today, and if I have done any good, accept it. Guard me during my rest and deliver me from all dangers. May Your grace be always with me and with all who are dear to me. Amen. \n\nBrief examination of conscience. \n\nAct of Contrition: \nMy Jesus, my good Jesus, who died for me on the Cross, forgive my sins, I do not want to sin anymore. Amen. \n\nAct of Faith:\nI firmly believe that there is one God in three really distinct persons: Father, Son, and Holy Spirit, who gives heaven to the good and hell to the wicked forever. I believe that the Son of God became man, suffered and died on the cross to save us, and rose again on the third day. I believe all that the Holy Catholic, Apostolic, Roman Church believes and teaches, because God, infallible truth, has revealed it. And in this belief I wish to live and die.\n\nAct of Hope:\nI hope, my God, with firm confidence, that by the merits of my Lord Jesus Christ You will give me eternal salvation and the graces necessary to obtain it, because You, supremely good and powerful, have promised it to those who faithfully observe Your commandments, as I propose to do with Your help.\n\nAct of Charity:\nI love You, my God, with all my heart and above all things, because You are infinitely good and lovable, and I would rather lose everything than offend You. For love of You, I love my neighbor as myself.",
  "prayerStudiesTitle": "Prayer Before Study",
  "prayerStudiesContent": "Ineffable Creator, You who are the true source of light and wisdom, deign to infuse the ray of Your brightness into the darkness of my intellect, removing from me the double darkness in which I was born: sin and ignorance.\n\nYou, who make eloquent the tongues of children, fashion my tongue and pour upon my lips the grace of Your blessing. Give me keenness to understand, capacity to retain, method and facility to learn, subtlety to interpret, and abundant grace to speak.\n\nGive me right beginning, direction in progressing, and perfection in concluding. Amen.\n(St. Thomas Aquinas)",
  "prayerMealsTitle": "Grace Before Meals",
  "prayerMealsContent": "Bless us, O Lord, and these Thy gifts, which we are about to receive from Thy bounty, through Christ our Lord. Amen.",
  "prayerAngelusTitle": "The Angelus",
  "prayerAngelusContent": "℣. The Angel of the Lord declared unto Mary.\n℟. And she conceived of the Holy Spirit.\n\nHail Mary...\n\n℣. Behold the handmaid of the Lord.\n℟. Be it done unto me according to thy word.\n\nHail Mary...\n\n℣. And the Word was made flesh.\n℟. And dwelt among us.\n\nHail Mary...\n\n℣. Pray for us, O holy Mother of God.\n℟. That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.\n\nLet us pray:\nPour forth, we beseech Thee, O Lord, Thy grace into our hearts; that we, to whom the incarnation of Christ, Thy Son, was made known by the message of an angel, may by His Passion and Cross be brought to the glory of His Resurrection, through the same Christ Our Lord. Amen.",
  "prayerReginaCaeliTitle": "Regina Caeli",
  "prayerReginaCaeliContent": "℣. Queen of Heaven, rejoice, alleluia.\n℟. For He whom you did merit to bear, alleluia.\n℣. Has risen, as he said, alleluia.\n℟. Pray for us to God, alleluia.\n\n℣. Rejoice and be glad, O Virgin Mary, alleluia.\n℟. For the Lord has truly risen, alleluia.\n\nLet us pray:\nO God, who gave joy to the world through the resurrection of Thy Son, our Lord Jesus Christ, grant we beseech Thee, that through the intercession of the Virgin Mary, His Mother, we may obtain the joys of everlasting life. Through the same Christ our Lord. Amen.",
  "prayerGuardianAngelTitle": "Guardian Angel Prayer",
  "prayerGuardianAngelContent": "Angel of God, my guardian dear, to whom God's love commits me here, ever this day be at my side, to light and guard, to rule and guide. Amen.",
  "prayerGuardianAngelContentLatin": "Angele Dei, qui custos es mei, me, tibi commissum pietate superna, illumina, custodi, rege et guberna. Amen.",
  "prayerStJosephTitle": "Prayer to St. Joseph",
  "prayerStJosephContent": "To you, O blessed Joseph, do we come in our tribulation, and having implored the help of your most holy Spouse, we confidently invoke your patronage also.\n\nThrough that charity which bound you to the Immaculate Virgin Mother of God and through the paternal love with which you embraced the Child Jesus, we humbly beg you graciously to regard the inheritance which Jesus Christ has purchased by his Blood, and with your power and strength to aid us in our necessities.\n\nO most watchful guardian of the Holy Family, defend the chosen children of Jesus Christ; O most loving father, ward off from us every contagion of error and corrupting influence; O our most mighty protector, be kind to us and from heaven assist us in our struggle with the power of darkness.\n\nAs once you rescued the Child Jesus from deadly peril, so now protect God's Holy Church from the snares of the enemy and from all adversity; shield, too, each one of us by your constant protection, so that, supported by your example and your aid, we may be able to live piously, to die in holiness, and to obtain eternal happiness in heaven. Amen.",
  "prayerStThereseTitle": "Prayer to St. Therese",
  "prayerStThereseContent": "O Little Therese of the Child Jesus, model of humility, confidence and love! From the heights of heaven, shower upon us these roses that you carry in your arms: the rose of humility, so that we may overcome our pride and accept the yoke of the Gospel; the rose of confidence, so that we may abandon ourselves to the will of God; the rose of love, so that, opening our souls without measure to grace, we may fulfill the only end for which God created us: To love Him and to make Him loved.\n\nYou who said: \"I will spend my heaven doing good on earth\", help me in my distress and succor me in this necessity. Amen.",
  "prayerGuadalupeTitle": "Prayer to Our Lady of Guadalupe",
  "prayerGuadalupeContent": "O Our Lady of Guadalupe, Mystical Rose, make intercession for Holy Church, protect the Sovereign Pontiff, and help all those who invoke thee in their necessities.\n\nAnd since thou art the ever Virgin Mary and Mother of the true God, obtain for us from thy most holy Son the grace of keeping our faith, sweet hope in the midst of the bitterness of life, burning charity, and the precious gift of final perseverance. Amen.\n(Pope Saint Pius X)",
  "prayerCarloAcutisTitle": "Prayer to Blessed Carlo Acutis",
  "prayerCarloAcutisContent": "Lord God, who filled the heart of young Saint Carlo Acutis with Your graces, kindling in him an ardent love for the Most Holy Eucharist and a tender filial devotion to the Virgin Mary, grant us the grace to imitate his example.\n\nThrough his intercession, teach us to seek Your Kingdom first, to approach the sacraments of Confession and Holy Communion with purity of soul, and to use the goods of this world solely for Your greater glory and the relief of the poor and needy.\n\nSaint Carlo Acutis, pray for us, that we may live ever united to Jesus and attain eternal life. Amen.",
  "temptationFightTitle": "Fight Against Temptation",
  "temptationFightDesc": "Prayers and help in times of temptation",
  "temptationStep1Title": "Recognize the Temptation",
  "temptationStep1Desc": "Temptation is a real danger to the soul. Recognize it immediately and do not dialogue with it. The devil is cunning and uses hesitation to overcome us.",
  "temptationStep1Prayer": "\"Watch and pray that you may not enter into temptation.\" (Mt 26:41)",
  "temptationStep2Title": "Ejaculatory Prayers",
  "temptationStep2Desc": "Short and powerful prayers for moments of temptation. Repeat them with fervor until you feel the temptation subside.",
  "temptationStep2Prayer": "• Jesus and Mary, I love you, save souls.\n• My Jesus, mercy!\n• Jesus, meek and humble of heart, make our hearts like unto Thine.\n• Refuge of Sinners, pray for us.",
  "temptationStep3Title": "St. Michael the Archangel",
  "temptationStep3Desc": "The Prince of the Heavenly Host is our defender against the snares of the devil. Invoke him with confidence!",
  "temptationStep3Prayer": "St. Michael the Archangel, defend us in battle, be our protection against the wickedness and snares of the devil. May God rebuke him we humbly pray; and do thou, O Prince of the Heavenly host, by the power of God, cast into hell Satan and all the evil spirits who prowl about the world seeking the ruin of souls. Amen.",
  "temptationStep4Title": "The Memorare",
  "temptationStep4Desc": "The Virgin Mary never abandons those who have recourse to Her. Trust in her maternal intercession.",
  "temptationStep4Prayer": "Remember, O most gracious Virgin Mary, that never was it known that anyone who fled to thy protection, implored thy help, or sought thy intercession was left unaided. Inspired by this confidence, I fly unto thee, O Virgin of virgins, my Mother; to thee do I come, before thee I stand, sinful and sorrowful. O Mother of the Word Incarnate, despise not my petitions, but in thy mercy hear and answer me. Amen.",
  "temptationStep5Title": "Flight is Victory",
  "temptationStep5Desc": "In temptation against purity, victory consists in flight. Do not fight hand-to-hand with temptation – flee from it! The saints conquered by fleeing, not by confronting.",
  "temptationStep5Prayer": "\"Flee from immorality.\" (1 Cor 6:18)\n\n\"He that loveth danger shall perish in it.\" (Sir 3:27)",
  "temptationStep6Title": "Change the Environment",
  "temptationStep6Desc": "Practical tips to flee temptation:\n\n• Change your thoughts: occupy your mind with something neutral\n• Change your location: leave the tempting environment\n• Do a task: manual work, exercise, reading\n• Seek company: do not stay alone\n• Turn off devices: distance yourself from the occasion",
  "temptationStep6Prayer": "Lord, give me the wisdom to flee from occasions of sin and the strength to withdraw from danger.",
  "temptationStep7Title": "Break the Siege",
  "temptationStep7Desc": "Aspirations for when discouragement attacks. Do not give up! God allows temptation to strengthen us, not to bring us down.",
  "temptationStep7Prayer": "• Lord, I believe! Help my unbelief.\n• Most Holy Mother, do not abandon me!\n• Sacred Heart of Jesus, I trust in You!\n• St. Joseph, guardian of purity, pray for us!",
  "temptationStep8Title": "Resolution and Consecration",
  "temptationStep8Desc": "Renew your purpose of fidelity to God. Consecrate yourself to the protection of Our Lady.",
  "temptationStep8Prayer": "O my Lady and my Mother, I offer myself entirely to you, and as a proof of my devotion, I consecrate to you this day my eyes, my ears, my mouth, my heart, and my whole being. And since I am yours, O incomparable Mother, guard me and defend me as your own possession. Amen.",
  "joyful1Title": "1st Mystery: The Annunciation",
  "joyful1Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, a profound humility of heart.",
  "joyful1Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this first decade in honor of Thine Incarnation in the womb of Mary; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through her intercession, a profound humility of heart. Amen.",
  "joyful2Title": "2nd Mystery: The Visitation",
  "joyful2Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, perfect charity toward our neighbor.",
  "joyful2Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this second decade in honor of the Visitation of Thy Most Holy Mother to her cousin Saint Elizabeth and the sanctification of Saint John the Baptist; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through the intercession of Thy Most Holy Mother, perfect charity toward our neighbor. Amen.",
  "joyful3Title": "3rd Mystery: The Nativity",
  "joyful3Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, detachment from material goods and love of poverty.",
  "joyful3Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this third decade in honor of Thy Nativity in the stable of Bethlehem; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through the intercession of Thy Most Holy Mother, detachment from earthly goods, detachment from ourselves, and love of poverty and of the poor. Amen.",
  "joyful4Title": "4th Mystery: The Presentation",
  "joyful4Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, great purity and perfect obedience.",
  "joyful4Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this fourth decade in honor of Thy Presentation in the Temple and the Purification of Mary; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through her intercession, great purity of body and soul and perfect obedience to the holy will of God. Amen.",
  "joyful5Title": "5th Mystery: The Finding in the Temple",
  "joyful5Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, true wisdom and conversion of life.",
  "joyful5Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this fifth decade in honor of Thy Finding in the Temple by Mary; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through her intercession, true wisdom, the conversion of our life, and that of all sinners. Amen.",
  "sorrowful1Title": "1st Mystery: The Agony in the Garden",
  "sorrowful1Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, contrition for our sins and conformity to the will of God.",
  "sorrowful1Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this first decade of the Sorrowful Mysteries in honor of Thy mortal Agony in the Garden of Olives; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through the intercession of Thy Most Holy Mother, contrition for our sins and perfect conformity to Thy holy will. Amen.",
  "sorrowful2Title": "2nd Mystery: The Scourging at the Pillar",
  "sorrowful2Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, mortification of our senses and perfect chastity.",
  "sorrowful2Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this second decade of the Sorrowful Mysteries in honor of Thy cruel Scourging; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through the intercession of Thy Most Holy Mother, the mortification of our senses and perfect chastity. Amen.",
  "sorrowful3Title": "3rd Mystery: The Crowning with Thorns",
  "sorrowful3Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, contempt for the world and detachment from vanities.",
  "sorrowful3Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this third decade of the Sorrowful Mysteries in honor of Thy Crowning with Thorns; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through the intercession of Thy Most Holy Mother, contempt for the world and detachment from honors and vanities. Amen.",
  "sorrowful4Title": "4th Mystery: The Carrying of the Cross",
  "sorrowful4Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, great patience in carrying our cross.",
  "sorrowful4Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this fourth decade of the Sorrowful Mysteries in honor of the carrying of Thy heavy Cross; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through the intercession of Thy Most Holy Mother, great patience to carry our cross after Thine example all the days of our life. Amen.",
  "sorrowful5Title": "5th Mystery: The Crucifixion and Death",
  "sorrowful5Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, the conversion of sinners and final perseverance.",
  "sorrowful5Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this fifth decade of the Sorrowful Mysteries in honor of Thy Crucifixion and sorrowful death on Calvary; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through the intercession of Thy Most Holy Mother, the conversion of sinners, our final perseverance, and the relief of the souls in Purgatory. Amen.",
  "glorious1Title": "1st Mystery: The Resurrection",
  "glorious1Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, a lively faith.",
  "glorious1Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this first decade of the Glorious Mysteries in honor of Thy glorious Resurrection; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through the intercession of Thy Most Holy Mother, a lively faith. Amen.",
  "glorious2Title": "2nd Mystery: The Ascension",
  "glorious2Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, a firm desire for Heaven and great trust in God.",
  "glorious2Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this second decade of the Glorious Mysteries in honor of Thy glorious Ascension into Heaven; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through the intercession of Thy Most Holy Mother, a firm desire for Heaven and great trust in Thee. Amen.",
  "glorious3Title": "3rd Mystery: The Descent of the Holy Spirit",
  "glorious3Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, the descent of the Holy Spirit and divine charity.",
  "glorious3Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this third decade of the Glorious Mysteries in honor of the mystery of Pentecost; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through the intercession of Thy Most Holy Mother, the descent of the Holy Spirit into our souls and the gift of true divine charity. Amen.",
  "glorious4Title": "4th Mystery: The Assumption",
  "glorious4Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, perfect union with her and tender devotion to so good a Mother.",
  "glorious4Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this fourth decade of the Glorious Mysteries in honor of the glorious Assumption of Thy Most Holy Mother into Heaven; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through her intercession, a perfect union with her and tender devotion to so good a Mother. Amen.",
  "glorious5Title": "5th Mystery: The Coronation",
  "glorious5Short": "We ask, through this mystery and through the intercession of Mary, perseverance in grace and the crown of eternal glory.",
  "glorious5Full": "We offer Thee, O Lord Jesus, this fifth decade of the Glorious Mysteries in honor of the Coronation of Thy Most Holy Mother in Heaven; and we ask of Thee, through this mystery and through her intercession, perseverance in grace and the crown of eternal glory. Amen.",
  "luminous1Title": "1st Mystery: The Baptism in the Jordan",
  "luminous1Short": "Jesus is baptized by John in the River Jordan. The heavens open, the Holy Spirit descends like a dove, and the Father declares: \"This is my beloved Son.\"",
  "luminous1Full": "Then cometh Jesus from Galilee to the Jordan, unto John, to be baptized by him. But John stayed him, saying: \"I ought to be baptized by thee, and comest thou to me?\" And Jesus answering, said to him: \"Suffer it to be so now. For so it becometh us to fulfill all justice.\" Then he suffered him. And Jesus being baptized, forthwith came out of the water: and lo, the heavens were opened to him: and he saw the Spirit of God descending as a dove, and coming upon him. And a voice came from the heavens, saying: \"This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.\" In this mystery, we contemplate the humility of Jesus, who did not need baptism, yet willed to sanctify the waters and give us an example. It is also the epiphany of the Most Holy Trinity: the Father who speaks, the Son who is baptized, and the Holy Spirit who descends.",
  "luminous2Title": "2nd Mystery: The Wedding at Cana",
  "luminous2Short": "At the wedding in Cana, Jesus performs His first miracle, turning water into wine, through the intercession of His Mother Mary.",
  "luminous2Full": "And the third day, there was a marriage in Cana of Galilee: and the mother of Jesus was there. And Jesus also was invited, and his disciples, to the marriage. And the wine failing, the mother of Jesus saith to him: \"They have no wine.\" And Jesus saith to her: \"Woman, what is that to me and to thee? my hour is not yet come.\" His mother saith to the waiters: \"Whatsoever he shall say to you, do ye.\" Now there were set there six waterpots of stone, according to the manner of the purifying of the Jews, containing two or three measures apiece. Jesus saith to them: \"Fill the waterpots with water.\" And they filled them up to the brim. And Jesus saith to them: \"Draw out now, and carry to the chief steward of the feast.\" And they carried it. And when the chief steward had tasted the water made wine, and knew not whence it was, but the waiters knew who had drawn the water; the chief steward calleth the bridegroom, and saith to him: \"Every man at first setteth forth good wine, and when men have well drunk, then that which is worse. But thou hast kept the good wine until now.\" This beginning of miracles did Jesus in Cana of Galilee; and manifested his glory, and his disciples believed in him.",
  "luminous3Title": "3rd Mystery: The Proclamation of the Kingdom",
  "luminous3Short": "Jesus travels through Galilee preaching the Gospel and calling for conversion: \"The kingdom of God is at hand: repent, and believe the gospel.\"",
  "luminous3Full": "And after that John was delivered up, Jesus came into Galilee, preaching the gospel of the kingdom of God, and saying: \"The time is accomplished, and the kingdom of God is at hand: repent, and believe the gospel.\" And Jesus went about all Galilee, teaching in their synagogues, and preaching the gospel of the kingdom: and healing all manner of sickness and every infirmity, among the people. And his fame went throughout all Syria, and they presented to him all sick people that were taken with divers diseases and torments, and such as were possessed by devils, and lunatics, and those that had palsy, and he cured them: and much people followed him from Galilee, and from Decapolis, and from Jerusalem, and from Judea, and from beyond the Jordan. And seeing the multitudes, he went up into a mountain, and when he was set down, his disciples came unto him. And opening his mouth, he taught them, saying: \"Blessed are the poor in spirit: for theirs is the kingdom of heaven. Blessed are they that mourn: for they shall be comforted.\"",
  "luminous4Title": "4th Mystery: The Transfiguration",
  "luminous4Short": "On Mount Tabor, Jesus is transfigured before Peter, James, and John. His face shines like the sun and His garments become white as light.",
  "luminous4Full": "And after six days Jesus taketh with him Peter and James and John, and leadeth them up into an high mountain apart by themselves, and was transfigured before them. And his garments became shining and exceeding white as snow, so as no fuller upon earth can make white. And there appeared to them Elias with Moses; and they were talking with Jesus. And Peter answering, said to Jesus: \"Rabbi, it is good for us to be here: and let us make three tabernacles, one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias.\" For he knew not what he said: for they were struck with fear. And there was a cloud overshadowing them: and a voice came out of the cloud, saying: \"This is my most beloved son; hear ye him.\" And immediately looking about, they saw no man any more, but Jesus only with them. And as they came down from the mountain, he charged them not to tell any man what things they had seen, till the Son of man shall be risen again from the dead.",
  "luminous5Title": "5th Mystery: The Institution of the Eucharist",
  "luminous5Short": "At the Last Supper, Jesus institutes the Eucharist, giving us His Body and Blood: \"This is my Body. Do this in memory of me.\"",
  "luminous5Full": "Now on the first day of the unleavened bread, when they sacrificed the pasch, the disciples say to him: \"Whither wilt thou that we go, and prepare for thee to eat the pasch?\" And whilst they were eating, Jesus took bread; and blessing, broke, and gave to them, and said: \"Take ye. This is my body.\" And having taken the chalice, giving thanks, he gave it to them. And they all drank of it. And he said to them: \"This is my blood of the new testament, which shall be shed for many. Amen I say to you, that I will drink no more of the fruit of the vine, until that day when I shall drink it new in the kingdom of God.\" Before the festival day of the pasch, Jesus knowing that his hour was come, that he should pass out of this world to the Father: having loved his own who were in the world, he loved them unto the end. This is the greatest gift: Jesus remains with us in the Eucharist until the end of time.",
  "prayerGloriaTitle": "Gloria Patri (Glory Be)",
  "prayerGloriaContent": "Glory be to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit. As it was in the beginning, is now, and ever shall be, world without end. Amen.",
  "prayerGloriaContentLatin": "Gloria Patri, et Filio, et Spiritui Sancto. Sicut erat in principio, et nunc, et semper, et in saecula saeculorum. Amen.",
  "prayerSalveTitle": "Salve Regina (Hail Holy Queen)",
  "prayerSalveContent": "Hail, holy Queen, Mother of mercy, our life, our sweetness, and our hope. To thee do we cry, poor banished children of Eve. To thee do we send up our sighs, mourning and weeping in this valley of tears. Turn then, most gracious Advocate, thine eyes of mercy toward us. And after this our exile, show unto us the blessed fruit of thy womb, Jesus. O clement, O loving, O sweet Virgin Mary.\n\n℣. Pray for us, O holy Mother of God,\n℟. that we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ. Amen.",
  "prayerSalveContentLatin": "Infinitas gratias tibi agimus, suprema Regina, pro beneficiis quae quotidie ex manibus tuis liberalibus accipimus. Dignare nunc et in aeternum nos sub potenti tuo patrocinio suscipere, et tibi gratias agentes, te Salve Regina salutamus.\n\nSalve, Regina, mater misericordiae, vita, dulcedo, et spes nostra, salve. Ad te clamamus, exsules filii Hevae. Ad te suspiramus, gementes et flentes in hac lacrimarum valle. Eia, ergo, advocata nostra, illos tuos misericordes oculos ad nos converte. Et Iesum, benedictum fructum ventris tui, nobis post hoc exsilium ostende. O clemens, O pia, O dulcis Virgo Maria.\n\n℣. Ora pro nobis, sancta Dei Genetrix.\n℟. Ut digni efficiamur promissionibus Christi. Amen.",
  "prayerFatimaTitle": "Fatima Prayer",
  "prayerFatimaContent": "O my Jesus, forgive us our sins, save us from the fires of hell, lead all souls to Heaven, especially those most in need of Thy mercy.",
  "prayerMariaImaculadaTitle": "Prayer Before Sleep",
  "prayerMariaImaculadaContent": "O Mary conceived without sin, deliver us this night from every mortal and venial sin, and from every imperfection. Amen.",
  "prayerMariaImaculadaContentLatin": "O Maria, sine labe concepta, libera nos hac nocte ab omni peccato mortali, veniali et ab omni imperfectione. Amen.",
  "prayerMariaImaculadaMorningTitle": "Morning Prayer to Mary",
  "prayerMariaImaculadaMorningContent": "O Mary conceived without sin, deliver us this day from every mortal and venial sin, and from every imperfection. Amen.",
  "prayerMariaImaculadaMorningContentLatin": "O Maria, sine labe concepta, libera nos hoc die ab omni peccato mortali, veniali et ab omni imperfectione. Amen.",
  "prayerSignCrossTitle": "Sign of the Cross",
  "prayerSignCrossContent": "In the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit. Amen.",
  "prayerSignCrossContentLatin": "In nomine Patris, et Filii, et Spiritus Sancti. Amen.",
