  "novenaCarloAcutisTitle": "Novena to St. Carlo Acutis",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDesc": "Patron of youth and the internet",
  "novenaCarloAcutisIcon": "computer",
  "novenaCarloAcutisOpening": "O eternal and merciful God, who manifest Your glory in the holiness of the little and the humble, we praise You for the Christian virtues with which You adorned the life of Saint Carlo Acutis. Through his intercession, we humbly beseech You to grant us the grace we ardently ask in this novena, if it be for Your honor and the salvation of our souls. (Make your petition). Through Christ our Lord. Amen.",
  "novenaCarloAcutisClosing": "Lord Jesus Christ, living bread come down from Heaven, who were the center of the life and the treasure of the heart of Saint Carlo Acutis, enkindle our souls also with love for Your tabernacle and fidelity to Holy Church. Through the intercession of Most Holy Mary and Saint Carlo Acutis, keep us in Your grace until the hour of death. Amen.",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay1Title": "Day 1 - Love of God Above All Things",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay1Meditation": "Saint Carlo Acutis, who from childhood placed the divine will above earthly desires, obtain for us detachment from the world and the sincere wish to please God alone. Amen.",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay2Title": "Day 2 - Constant Union with Jesus",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay2Meditation": "Saint Carlo Acutis, who made friendship with Our Lord the rule of every moment of your day, obtain for us the grace to walk in God's presence in all our actions. Amen.",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay3Title": "Day 3 - Devotion to the Holy Guardian Angel",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay3Meditation": "Saint Carlo Acutis, who fostered filial trust in the holy Angels sent by God to guard us, teach us to heed our Guardian Angel and flee every occasion of sin. Amen.",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay4Title": "Day 4 - Purity of Soul and Frequent Confession",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay4Meditation": "Saint Carlo Acutis, who diligently sought the sacrament of Penance to keep your baptismal robe unstained, obtain for us true contrition and a firm purpose of amendment. Amen.",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay5Title": "Day 5 - Joy Born of Contemplation",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay5Meditation": "Saint Carlo Acutis, who found true Christian joy in prayer and forgetfulness of self, deliver us from selfishness and turn our eyes toward eternal goods. Amen.",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay6Title": "Day 6 - Ardent Desire for Holiness",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay6Meditation": "Saint Carlo Acutis, who asked nothing of God other than to correspond faithfully to the call to holiness, kindle in us a hunger and thirst for evangelical perfection. Amen.",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay7Title": "Day 7 - Filial Piety toward the Virgin Mary",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay7Meditation": "Saint Carlo Acutis, who daily honored the Mother of God with the devout recitation of the Holy Rosary, obtain for us tender trust in Mary's maternal protection. Amen.",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay8Title": "Day 8 - Fervor before the Most Holy Eucharist",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay8Meditation": "Saint Carlo Acutis, who adored Jesus truly present in the Most Blessed Sacrament and spread faith in Eucharistic miracles, increase in us a lively faith in the Altar. Amen.",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay9Title": "Day 9 - Charity toward the Poor and Final Perseverance",
  "novenaCarloAcutisDay9Meditation": "Saint Carlo Acutis, who assisted the needy and offered your final sufferings for the Church and the Pope, obtain for us the grace of final perseverance and a holy death. Amen.",
  "novenaOpeningPrayerLabel": "OPENING PRAYER",
  "novenaMeditationLabel": "DAY'S MEDITATION",
  "novenaPrayersLabel": "PRAYERS",
  "novenaClosingPrayerLabel": "CLOSING PRAYER",
  "novenaTeresaTitle": "Novena of the Roses",
  "novenaTeresaDesc": "St. Thérèse of the Child Jesus",
  "novenaTeresaOpening": "Most Holy Trinity, Father, Son, and Holy Spirit, I thank You for all the favors, all the graces with which You enriched the soul of Your servant Thérèse of the Child Jesus during the 24 years she spent on Earth. Through the merits of this dear little saint, grant me the grace I ardently ask (make your petition), if it is according to Your most holy will and for the salvation of my soul. Strengthen my faith and my hope, O Saint Thérèse, fulfilling once more your promise that no one would invoke you in vain, making me gain a rose, a sign that I will obtain the grace requested.",
  "novenaTeresaPrayers": "Then, pray 24 times: Glory be to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit, as it was in the beginning, is now, and ever shall be, world without end. Amen!\n\nTo each Glory Be you can add the aspiration:\n\nSt. Thérèse of the Child Jesus, pray for us!\n\nLet us pray:\nOur Father and Hail Mary.",
  "novenaTeresaDay1Title": "\"For me, prayer is a surge of the heart; it is a simple look turned toward heaven, it is a cry of recognition and of love, embracing both trial and joy. In a word, it is something great, something supernatural, which expands my soul and unites me to Jesus.\"",
  "novenaTeresaDay2Title": "\"Perfection consists in doing His will, in being what He wills us to be.\"",
  "novenaTeresaDay3Title": "\"What draws me to my heavenly home is the thought that I can ignite in the love of God a multitude of souls who will bless Him eternally.\"",
  "novenaTeresaDay4Title": "\"How great is the power of prayer! It is like a queen having at each instant free access to the king and able to obtain whatever she asks.\"",
  "novenaTeresaDay5Title": "\"I prefer neither to die nor to live… What God prefers and chooses for me, that is what pleases me more.\"",
  "novenaTeresaDay6Title": "\"After my death, I will let fall a shower of roses from heaven.\"",
  "novenaTeresaDay7Title": "\"When I get to heaven, how many graces I will ask for you! I will torment Our Lord so much that, if He at first thinks of refusing me, my insistence will force Him to grant my desires.\"",
  "novenaTeresaDay8Title": "\"Charity must not consist in feelings but in works.\"",
  "novenaTeresaDay9Title": "\"I want to spend my heaven doing good on earth. I will not look upon souls only, but I will come down to them. My mission will begin: to teach men to love God as I love Him. I will rest only at the end of the world when the number of the elect is complete.\"",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoTitle": "Novena to the Sacred Heart",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDesc": "In honor of the Heart of Jesus",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoOpening": "Remember, O most sweet Jesus, that never was it known that anyone who fled to Thy protection, implored Thy help, or sought Thy intercession was left unaided. Inspired with this confidence, I fly unto Thee, O Sacred Heart of Jesus, King and center of all hearts, I come to Thee, and groaning under the weight of my sins, I prostrate myself before Thee. My Jesus, by Thy precious Blood and the love of Thy divine Heart, despise not my supplications, but graciously hear and answer me. Amen.",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoClosing": "Most sweet Heart of Jesus, Thy precious Blood is the life of my soul; in Thee alone I wish to live, Thee alone I wish to love and serve. By the burning thirst Thou hast to save me, enlighten my mind with the light of Thy divine grace. Sanctify my heart, strengthen my will, forgive my sins, and heal all my miseries. Increase my faith, fortify my hope, and kindle in me ever more the fire of Thy holy love. Grant me, finally, all the graces I hope to obtain through this novena. O most sweet Jesus, live in me now and forever. Amen.\n\n℣. Sweet Heart of Jesus,\n℟. make me love Thee more and more!",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoPrayers": "Our Father, Hail Mary, and Glory Be.\n\n℣. Jesus, meek and humble of heart,\n℟. Make our hearts like unto Thine.",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay1Title": "Heart of Jesus, Temple of the Most Holy Trinity",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay1Meditation": "Consider, my soul, how the Heart of Jesus was the most sacred temple that the Most Holy and Blessed Trinity had in this world. One act of love or reverence, or adoration, or any other virtue that came from this Heart united to the Person of the Divine Word was infinitely more esteemed by God than all the acts that all creatures in the world could form, even if all were burning seraphim. Consider, then, my soul, what increases of glory the Most Holy Trinity had with the adorations and praises that Jesus Christ gave Him in this temple? And if you, my soul, must also be a temple of the Most Holy Trinity by grace, ask this Lord to make your heart like unto this most ardent Heart.",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay2Title": "Heart of Jesus, Artisan of the Most Holy Sacrament",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay2Meditation": "Consider, my soul, that from the sovereign Heart of Jesus came the Most Divine Sacrament, where we have deposited the most sacred Blood that flowed from His side; and such was the refinement of the Heart of Jesus, as the Lord said to one of His servants, that if He had not left Himself in the Most Holy Sacrament, He could not have died on the Cross. So attached was that loving Heart to men that, impatient of absences, seeing that He had to depart to the Father, He invented this loving device of departing and remaining at the same time, of glorifying the saints in Heaven and keeping us company on earth. Consider, my soul, how much you owe to the burning Heart of your Lord, and be confounded for thanking Him so little for realizing, with the institution of the Most Holy Sacrament, the idea of a good work by which He communicates infinite goods to you.",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay3Title": "Heart of Jesus, Bush of Penetrating Thorns",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay3Meditation": "Consider, my soul, that from the moment the breaths of life began in this Heart, until they were exhaled in death, this innocent Heart never lived without sorrows, because, as soon as it was animated, it accepted the precept of suffering for men; with life its sorrows began. Before the exterior torments arrived, Jesus suffered interiorly the sorrows, seeing the great offenses that men committed against His Eternal Father. In the Garden, the representation of His sorrows was so vivid that His blood broke through all His pores. And if the sorrows merely considered caused Him so much bitterness, what would they be when truly suffered? Confound yourself, my soul, for the lukewarmness with which you love this Divine Heart, and for the negligence with which you do not imitate it, since suffering so repels you, and you flee so much from mortification.",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay4Title": "Heart of Jesus, Most Burning Furnace of Charity",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay4Meditation": "Consider, my soul, that the extreme with which this Sacred Heart loved and loves God, only God Himself can comprehend. The chest was a furnace of fires, the Heart was a mine of flames that rose so high that they ended in God. This most ardent Heart came to earth to set it on fire, and the world being so great, there would still be fires left over, if the world were infinitely larger. The rare kindnesses that the Lord worked for us and the continuous benefits He is doing for us are all flames that continually come out of that furnace of most burning charity. And is it possible, my soul, that seeing your heart surrounded by as many flames as there are benefits you receive from the Heart of Jesus, it is still so cold and lukewarm?",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay5Title": "Heart of Jesus, Paradise of Heavenly Delights",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay5Meditation": "Consider, my soul, that in this most sweet Heart are enclosed all the delights of Paradise. It is the sea where they enter, and from where all the rivers of divine regalements come out; they enter it, communicated by God, and come out of it to delight just souls. In this paradise of the Heart of Jesus, the Lord gave entrance to many saints who excelled in eminent virtues, and seeing themselves almost submerged in a sea of consolations, they asked the Lord to moderate them, because without fainting they could not bear such excessive abundance. Poor you, my soul, who participate so little in these riches! But why are you surprised, if you do not love that center of love? Learn to love it, and you will make yourself worthy of the delights of this paradise.",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay6Title": "Heart of Jesus, Most Rich Treasury of Graces",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay6Meditation": "Consider, my soul, that just as a treasure is an aggregate of many riches, so the Heart of Jesus is a deposit of infinite graces. Here you will find supreme innocence, deepest humility, immense fortitude, endless wisdom; and finally, to make a concept of the graces and riches of this treasure, you must first consider who communicated them and to whom they were communicated. The Eternal Father was the one who communicated them, and the Son of God was the one to whom they were communicated. And the Eternal Father having infinite liberality, what graces would the Son of God receive from this infinite liberality? Here judgment is lost and human consideration is abyssed. My soul, if the graces of this treasure are so many, love this Heart so that you can participate in its riches.",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay7Title": "Heart of Jesus, Abyss of Immense Pity",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay7Meditation": "Consider, my soul, that this loving Heart is so pitying that it denies its pity to no one; so much so that, if any afflicted soul turns to Him with lively faith, He immediately runs to console it with His remedy; so much so that, when He sees someone distressed, He immediately runs, pitying, with His affection to help them. Seeing Himself offended by our faults, He dissimulates everything, and waits for our repentance to forgive us. If after repenting we fall again into the same miseries, His patience does not tire, His mercy is not exhausted, the doors of His pity do not close, but rather He seeks us with aids and calls us with repeated inspirations, and if we turn to Him, He immediately rejoices and is well with us. And believing you, my soul, all this, do you not die of love for this Heart?",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay8Title": "Heart of Jesus, Attraction of Our Hearts",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay8Meditation": "Consider, my soul, what Our Lord said: that only after being exalted on the Cross, and not before, would His side be opened, thus leaving His loving Heart open. Because the Lord judged that whoever set his eyes on it, attracted by a very sweet violence, would certainly surrender. And if you, my soul, do not surrender, it is because you do not set your eyes on it. If you saw that from this Heart flow the heavenly truths, with which the darkness of faults are dispelled; if you saw that from it flows the fire that burns cold souls, the lights that banish our ignorance, the mercies that wash our faults, the sweetness, the aids, the inspirations... and finally, if you saw that from this Heart flows every good, would you leave, my soul, to love this Heart? Would you leave to be caught in the bonds of so much love?",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay9Title": "Heart of Jesus, Pledge of Eternal Life",
  "novenaSagradoCoracaoDay9Meditation": "Consider, my soul, that just as the human heart is the principle of temporal life, so the Heart of Jesus is for us the principle of eternal life; because, if for eternal life the forgiveness of faults and the remission of sins are necessary, from this Heart coming blood and water, and we having the Blood of Christ as the foundation of our redemption, and in the water a representation of Baptism, without which no one enters glory, it follows from this that this Heart is the door through which all enter eternal life. Just as God there in Paradise gave life to man with a breath, so with another breath Christ infused into His disciples the grace of the Holy Spirit, because, as the breath from the mouth comes from the heart, Christ wanted to show that from His Heart comes grace. So, my soul, if you believe all this, know that if you love this Divine Heart, and imitate it, you will obtain grace, and will achieve glory in eternal life.",
  "novenaConceicaoTitle": "Novena to the Immaculate Conception",
  "novenaConceicaoDesc": "Traditional novena to Our Lady of the Immaculate Conception",
  "novenaConceicaoOpening": "Come, Holy Spirit, fill the hearts of Thy faithful and enkindle in them the fire of Thy love.\n℣. Send forth Thy Spirit, and they shall be created.\n℟. And Thou shalt renew the face of the earth.\n\nLet us pray.\nO God, who didst instruct the hearts of Thy faithful by the light of the Holy Spirit, grant us in the same Spirit to love what is right and ever to rejoice in His consolation. Through Christ our Lord. Amen.\n\nO most pure Virgin conceived without sin, from the first instant all beautiful and without stain. O glorious Mary, full of grace and Mother of my God, Queen of angels and men. I humbly venerate you as Mother of my Savior, who, being God, taught me with His esteem, respect, and submission to you the honor and homage I must render you. Deign to accept me, who in this novena consecrate myself to you. You being a safe refuge for repentant sinners, I have reason to have recourse to you; being Mother of mercy, you cannot but have compassion on my misery; being, after Jesus Christ, all my hope, you cannot but be pleased with the tender confidence I have in you. Make me worthy to call myself your child, so that I may confidently say: Show that you are Mother.",
  "novenaConceicaoClosing": "℣. You are all beautiful, Mary.\n℟. You are all beautiful, Mary.\n℣. And without original stain.\n℟. And without original stain.\n℣. You are the glory of Jerusalem.\n℟. You are the joy of Israel.\n℣. You are the honor of our people.\n℟. You are the Advocate of sinners.\n℣. O Mary.\n℟. O Mary.\n℣. Virgin most prudent.\n℟. Mother most clement.\n℣. Pray for us.\n℟. Intercede for us to the Lord Jesus Christ.\n\n℣. In your Conception, O Virgin, you were immaculate.\n℟. Pray for us to the Father whose Son you bore.\n\nLet us pray.\nO God, who by the Immaculate Conception of the Virgin Mary prepared a worthy dwelling for Your Son and, in view of the future merits of Christ's death, preserved her from all stain, grant us, through her intercession, the grace to come to You purified.\nO God, shepherd and guide of all the faithful, look favorably upon Your servant the Pope, whom You have constituted pastor of Your Church; grant him, we beseech You, to serve by word and example those whom he governs, so that he may attain eternal life with the flock entrusted to him.\nO God, our refuge and strength, hear the pious supplications of Your Church, You who are the author of piety, and grant us effectively to obtain what we confidently ask of You. Through Christ our Lord. Amen.",
  "novenaConceicaoPrayers": "Say one Hail Mary and one Glory Be.",
  "novenaConceicaoDay1Title": "First Day",
  "novenaConceicaoDay1Meditation": "Here I am at your most holy feet, O Immaculate Virgin. I greatly rejoice with you, chosen from eternity to be the Mother of the Eternal Word and preserved from original sin. I give thanks and bless the Most Holy Trinity, who enriched you with this privilege in your Conception, and I humbly beseech you to obtain for me the grace to overcome the sad consequences that original sin left in me. Make me overcome them and no longer fail to love my God.",
  "novenaConceicaoDay2Title": "Second Day",
  "novenaConceicaoDay2Meditation": "O Mary, immaculate lily of purity, I rejoice with you, who from the first instant of your Conception were filled with grace and received the perfect use of reason. I give thanks and adore the Most Holy Trinity, who granted you such sublime gifts. I am wholly confounded before you, seeing myself so poor in grace. You, who were fully filled with heavenly grace, make me participate and share in the treasures of your Immaculate Conception.",
  "novenaConceicaoDay3Title": "Third Day",
  "novenaConceicaoDay3Meditation": "O Mary, mystical rose of purity, I rejoice with you, who in your Immaculate Conception gloriously triumphed over the infernal serpent and were conceived without the stain of original sin. I give thanks and praise with all my heart to the Most Holy Trinity, who granted you such a privilege, and I beseech you to obtain for me the strength to overcome all the snares of the infernal enemy and not to stain my soul with sin. Always help me and make me, with your protection, always triumph over the common enemy of our eternal salvation.",
  "novenaConceicaoDay4Title": "Fourth Day",
  "novenaConceicaoDay4Meditation": "O Immaculate Virgin Mary, mirror of purity, I am filled with supreme joy to see that from your Conception the most sublime and perfect gifts of virtue and also all the gifts of the Holy Spirit were infused into you. I give thanks and praise to the Most Holy Trinity, who favored you with these privileges, and I beseech you, O benign Mother, to obtain for me the practice of virtue and the grace to become worthy of receiving the gifts and grace of the Holy Spirit.",
  "novenaConceicaoDay5Title": "Fifth Day",
  "novenaConceicaoDay5Meditation": "O Mary, resplendent moon of purity, I rejoice with you, for the mystery of your Immaculate Conception was the beginning of the salvation of the whole human race and the joy of the entire world. I give thanks and bless the Most Holy Trinity, who thus magnified and glorified you, and I beseech you to obtain for me the grace to know how to profit from the passion and death of your Jesus. May the Blood shed on the cross not be useless for me, but may I live holily and be saved.",
  "novenaConceicaoDay6Title": "Sixth Day",
  "novenaConceicaoDay6Meditation": "O Immaculate Mary, splendid star of purity, I rejoice with you, because your Immaculate Conception was a reason for the greatest joy for all the angels of paradise. I give thanks and bless the Most Holy Trinity, who enriched you with such a beautiful privilege. Make me one day enter into this joy and be able, in the company of the angels, to praise and bless you eternally.",
  "novenaConceicaoDay7Title": "Seventh Day",
  "novenaConceicaoDay7Meditation": "O Immaculate Mary, rising dawn of purity, I rejoice with you, amazed that at the very moment of your Conception you were confirmed in grace and made impeccable. I give thanks and exalt the Most Holy Trinity, who distinguished only you with this particular privilege. Obtain for me, O holy Virgin, a total and continual horror of sin, more than of any other evil, and that I prefer to die rather than sin again.",
  "novenaConceicaoDay8Title": "Eighth Day",
  "novenaConceicaoDay8Meditation": "O Virgin Mary, sun without stain, I rejoice with you, full of joy for having received from God in your Conception a grace greater and more copious than that achieved by all the angels and saints at the height of their merits. I give thanks to the Most Holy Trinity, amazed at the supreme beneficence with which it dispensed this privilege to you. Make me correspond to divine grace and no longer abuse it. Transform my heart and make me repent now of my faults.",
  "novenaConceicaoDay9Title": "Ninth Day",
  "novenaConceicaoDay9Meditation": "O Mary, Immaculate Virgin, living light of holiness, example of purity and my Mother. You, as soon as conceived, adored God profoundly and gave Him thanks, since through you, the ancient curse undone, the greatest blessing was poured out on the children of Adam. Make this blessing ignite in my heart an ardent love for God. Inflame it, so that I may love Him constantly and enjoy Him forever in paradise, where I can thank Him more ardently for the singular privileges He granted you and enjoy you crowned with so much glory.",
  "novenaNatalTitle": "Christmas Novena",
  "novenaNatalDesc": "Meditations by St. Alphonsus Liguori. A deep preparation to receive the Child Jesus.",
  "novenaNatalOpening": "Opening Hymn: Puer Natus\n(Or another Christmas hymn)",
  "novenaNatalClosing": "Closing Hymn: Adeste Fideles\n(Or another Christmas hymn)",
  "novenaNatalPrayers": "At the end of the meditation and prayer, pray the Rosary and the Litany of Our Lady.",
  "novenaNatalDay1Title": "First Day - December 16",
  "novenaNatalDay1Meditation": "GOD GAVE US HIS ONLY-BEGOTTEN SON AS SAVIOR\n\nBehold, I have given thee to be the light of the Gentiles, that thou mayst be my salvation even to the farthest part of the earth. (Is. 49:6)\n\nLet us consider how the eternal Father said to the Child Jesus at the moment of His conception these words: Son, I have given you to the world as light and life of the peoples, so that you may seek their salvation, which I esteem as much as if it were my own. It is necessary, therefore, that you commit yourself completely for the benefit of men. 'Given completely to men, and entirely delivered to their needs.' It is necessary that at birth you suffer extreme poverty, so that man may be enriched; it is necessary that you be sold as a slave, so that man may be free; it is necessary that, as a slave, you be scourged and crucified, to pay my justice the penalty due for men; it is necessary that you sacrifice blood and life, to free man from eternal death. Know, finally, that you are no longer yours, but man's. For a Child is born to us, and a son is given to us. Thus my beloved Son, man will return to love me and be mine, seeing that I give you entirely to him, my only-begotten Son, and that I have nothing more left to give him.\n\nSo God loved the world - oh, infinite love, worthy only of an infinite God - so God loved the world as to give his only begotten Son. The Child Jesus was not saddened by this proposal, but, on the contrary, took pleasure in it and accepted it with love and joy: 'He, as a bridegroom coming out of his bride chamber, hath rejoiced as a giant to run the way.' (Ps. 18:6) And from the first moment of His incarnation He gave Himself completely for man and gladly embraced all the sorrows and ignominies He was to suffer on earth for love of men. These were, according to St. Bernard, the hills and valleys that Jesus Christ had to traverse so quickly, according to the Song of Songs, to save men. Behold he cometh leaping upon the mountains, skipping over the hills.\n\nLet us reflect here how the Father, sending us His Son to be our Redeemer and to seal peace between Him and men, obliged Himself in a certain way to forgive us and to love us, by reason of the pact He made to receive us into His grace, since the Son satisfies His divine justice for us. In turn, the divine Word, having accepted the mission given to Him by the Father, who, sending Him to redeem us gave Him to us, also obliged Himself to love us, not for our merits, but to fulfill the pious will of His Father.",
  "novenaNatalDay2Title": "Second Day - December 17",
  "novenaNatalDay2Meditation": "THE AFFLICTION OF THE HEART OF JESUS IN THE WOMB OF MARY\n\nSacrifice and oblation thou wouldest not: but a body thou hast fitted to me. (Heb. 10:5)\n\nConsider the great bitterness with which the heart of the Child Jesus must have felt afflicted and oppressed in the womb of Mary, at that first instant when the Father proposed to Him the series of contempt, labors, and agonies He was to suffer in His life to free men from their miseries: 'In the morning he wakeneth my ear, that I may hear him as a master... I have not turned away back. I have given my body to the strikers.' (Is. 50:4-6) Thus spoke Jesus through the mouth of the Prophet: 'In the morning...', that is, from the first moment of my conception, my Father made me understand His will: that I should have a life of suffering and finally be sacrificed on the cross; 'I have not turned away back; I have given my body to the strikers.' And I accepted everything for the salvation of souls and, from then on, I gave my body to the scourges, to the nails, and to death.\n\nPonder then how much Jesus Christ suffered in His life and in His passion; everything was placed before His eyes from the womb of His Mother and everything He embraced with love; but, in consenting to this acceptance and overcoming the natural repugnance of the senses, how much anguish and oppression did the innocent Heart of Jesus have to suffer! He knew well what He first had to suffer; the sufferings and opprobrium of birth in a cold cave, stable of animals; the thirty years of work as a craftsman; the consideration that He would be treated by men as ignorant, slave, seducer, and guilty of the most infamous and painful death reserved for criminals.\n\nOur amiable Redeemer accepted everything at each moment, and at each moment He accepted it, He suffered united all the pains and dejections that He would later suffer until His death. The very knowledge of His divine dignity contributed to make Him feel more the insults received from men: 'My confusion is always before me.' He continually had before His eyes His shame, especially the confusion He would feel upon seeing Himself one day stripped, scourged, nailed with three iron nails, thus giving His life amid reproaches and curses from those who benefited from His death. 'Becoming obedient unto death, even to the death of the cross' (Phil. 2:8) and for what? To save us, miserable and ungrateful sinners.\n\nPRAYER\nOur beloved Redeemer, how much it cost You from the moment You entered the world to take us out of the abyss in which our sins had submerged us. To free us from the slavery of the devil, to which we voluntarily sold ourselves, You accepted to be treated as the worst of slaves; and we, who knew it, so many times had the audacity to embitter Your most amiable Heart, which loved us so much. But since You, our God, being innocent, accepted such a painful life and death, we accept for Your love, Jesus, all the pains that come from Your hands. We accept and embrace them because they come from those hands pierced one day to free us from hell, which we so often deserved. Your love, our Redeemer, in offering Yourself to suffer so much for us, obliges us to accept for You any pain and contempt. Give us, Lord, through Your merits, Your holy love, which makes all pains and all ignominies sweet for us. We love You above all things, we love You with all our heart, we love You more than ourselves. You, in Your life, gave us so many and so great proofs of affection and we, ungrateful, what proof of love do we give You? Make, then, O our God, that during the years that remain of our life we give You some proof of love. We would not dare, on the day of judgment, to appear before You as poor as we are now and without doing anything for Your love; but what can we do without Your grace? Only beg You to help us, and even that our supplication is Your grace. O Jesus, help us by the merit of Your pains and the blood You shed for me.\nMost Holy Mary, recommend us to Your Son, since for our love You had Him in your womb. Remember that we are of those souls for whom Your Son died.",
  "novenaNatalDay3Title": "Third Day - December 18",
  "novenaNatalDay3Meditation": "JESUS BECOMES A CHILD TO WIN OUR CONFIDENCE AND OUR LOVE\n\nA Child is born to us, and a son is given to us. (Is. 9:6)\n\nLet us consider how after so many centuries, after so many prayers and requests, the Messiah came, was born, and gave Himself entirely to us, whom the holy patriarchs and prophets were not worthy to see; the desire of the Gentiles, the desire of the everlasting hills, our Savior: 'A Child is born to us, and a son is given to us.' The Son of God made Himself small to make us great: He gave Himself to us so that we might give ourselves to Him; He came to show us His love, so that we might give Him ours. Let us receive Him, then, with affection, let us love Him and have recourse to Him in all our needs. Children, says St. Bernard, easily grant what is asked of them. Jesus came as a child, to show us that He is disposed to give us all His goods. 'In whom are hid all the treasures.' (Col. 2:3) 'The Father... hath given all things into his hand.' (Jn. 3:35) If we want light, He came to enlighten us; if we want strength to resist enemies, He came to strengthen us; if we want forgiveness and salvation, He came precisely to forgive and save us; if we want, in a word, the supreme gift of divine love, He came to inflame us; and for this, above all, He became a child and wanted to present Himself to us poor and humble, to appear more lovable, to take away all fear and conquer our affection: 'Thus should He come who wanted to banish fear and seek charity,' says St. Peter Chrysologus.\n\nMoreover, Jesus Christ wanted to come as a child, so that we might love Him not only with appreciative love, but with tender love. All children know how to conquer the affectionate affection of those around them, and who will not love with tenderness his God, seeing Him a little child, cold, poor, humiliated and abandoned, crying on the straw of a manger?\n\nCome to love God made child and made poor, and who is so lovable that He came down from heaven to give Himself completely to us.\n\nPRAYER\nO amiable Jesus, so despised by us! You came down from heaven to rescue us from hell and give Yourself completely to us, how could we so many times turn our backs on You, O God! Men are so grateful to creatures that if someone gives them a gift, sends them a greeting, gives them any proof of affection, they do not forget and feel obliged to correspond. And, on the contrary, they are so ungrateful to You, who are their God, and so lovable that for their love You did not refuse to give Your blood and life. But, woe to us, we were even worse than others, because we were more loved and more ungrateful. Ah! If the graces You gave us had been given to a heretic, an idolater, perhaps they would have been sanctified, and we offended You. Please, do not remember, Lord, the injuries we did to You. You said that when a sinner repents, You forget all the sins committed: 'None of his iniquities which he hath wrought shall be remembered unto him.' (Ez. 18:22) If in the past we did not love ourselves, in the future we want only to love You. Since You gave Yourself completely to us, we give You in exchange all our will; with it we love You and that we love You we want to repeat forever. We want to live repeating it and repeating it die, to begin from the moment we enter eternity to love You with a continuous love that will last eternally. Meanwhile, Lord, our only good and only love, we propose to put Your will before all our pleasures. For nothing do we want to stop loving who loved us so much; we no longer want to displease who deserves infinite love. Second, Jesus, our desire with Your grace.\nOur Queen, Mary, we acknowledge that all the graces received from God are due to your intercession; continue to intercede for us, obtain for us perseverance, you who are the Mother of all graces.",
  "novenaNatalDay4Title": "Fourth Day - December 19",
  "novenaNatalDay4Meditation": "THE PASSION OF JESUS CHRIST LASTED ALL HIS LIFE\n\nMy sorrow is continually before me. (Ps. 37:18)\n\nLet us consider how at that first instant when the soul of Jesus Christ was created and united to His body, in the womb of Mary, the Eternal Father showed His Son His will that He should die for the redemption of the world; and at that same instant He showed Him all the pains He was to suffer until death to redeem men. He then showed Him all the labors, contempt, and poverty He was to suffer in His life, both in Bethlehem and in Egypt and Nazareth, and then all the sorrows and ignominies of the passion: scourges, thorns, nails, and cross; all the tediums, sadness, agonies, and abandonments in the midst of which He was to end His life on Calvary.\n\nAbraham, leading his son to death, did not want to afflict him by telling him in advance that he would die, and that in the short time necessary to reach the mountain. But the Eternal Father wanted His incarnate Son, destined as a victim for our sins to His justice, to suffer immediately, by the knowledge of them, all the pains to which He would later have to submit Himself during His life and in His death. Hence, the sadness suffered by Jesus in the Garden, capable of taking His life, as He declared: 'My soul is sorrowful even unto death,' (Mt. 26:38) He also suffered it constantly from the first moment He was in the womb of His Mother. Thus, from then on He felt vividly and suffered the united weight of all the sorrows and reproaches that awaited Him.\n\nThe whole life and all the years of our Redeemer were full of sorrows and tears: 'My life is wasted with grief: and my years in sighs.' (Ps. 30:11) His divine Heart did not have a moment free from suffering; whether He watched or slept, worked or rested, prayed or spoke, He always had before His eyes that bitter representation, which tormented His most holy Soul more than all their pains tormented the holy martyrs. They suffered, but, helped by divine grace, they suffered with joy and fervor. Jesus Christ suffered, but He suffered always with His heart full of tedium and sadness, and He accepted everything for our love.\n\nPRAYER\nO sweet, O amiable, O loving Heart of Jesus, thus from childhood You were embittered and agonized in the womb of Mary? All this You suffered, Jesus, to atone for the penalty and eternal agony that we deserved to suffer in hell for our sins. You, then, suffered without any relief to save us, after we dared to abandon God and turn our backs on Him, to satisfy our miserable tastes. We thank You, loving and afflicted Heart of Our Lord. We thank You and have compassion on You considering that You suffered so much for men and that they do not have compassion on You. How great is the love of God and the ingratitude of men. O our Redeemer, how few are the men who think of Your sorrows and Your love. O God, how few are those who love You. And woe to us who also lived so many years without remembering You! You suffered so much that we might love You and we do not love You. Forgive us, Jesus, forgive us we want to amend ourselves and we want to love You. Woe to us, Lord, if we resist Your grace and by our resistance condemn ourselves. How many mercies You used with us and especially Your voice that now invites us to love You, would be our greatest pains in hell. Beloved Jesus, have pity on us, do not allow us to live more ungrateful to Your love; give us light and strength to overcome everything and to fulfill Your will. Hear us, we beseech You, by the merits of Your Passion.\nWe hope everything from You and from Your intercession, O Mary. Dear Mother, help us, You who obtained for us all the graces we received from God; continue to help us, for if You do not we will be unfaithful, as we were in the past. You are all our hope and all the reason for our confidence.",
  "novenaNatalDay5Title": "Fifth Day - December 20",
  "novenaNatalDay5Meditation": "JESUS CHRIST OFFERED HIMSELF FROM THE BEGINNING FOR OUR SALVATION\n\nHe was offered because it was his own will. (Is. 53:7)\n\nThe divine Word, from the first instant He saw Himself made man and child in the womb of Mary, offered Himself for the pains and death for the ransom of the world. He knew that all the sacrifices of lambs and bulls offered to God in antiquity had not been able to satisfy for the faults of men, but that it was necessary that a divine person satisfy for them the price of their redemption. For He said, as the Apostle affirms: 'Sacrifice and oblation thou wouldest not: but a body thou hast fitted to me. Then said I: Behold I come.' (Heb. 10:5-7) My Father, said Jesus Christ, all the victims that have been offered to You until now are not enough nor will be enough to satisfy Your justice; You have given me a passible body so that with the effusion of my blood You may be appeased and save men: behold, I am here, 'ecce venio', I accept everything and submit everything to Your will.\n\nThe inferior part of His will naturally experienced repugnance and refused to live and die amid so many sorrows and opprobrium, but the rational part, which was completely subordinated to the will of the Father, overcame and accepted everything, Jesus beginning to suffer from that moment, all the anguish and sorrows He would suffer in the years of His life, thus acted our divine Redeemer from the first instants of His entrance into the world.\n\nAnd how did we behave with Jesus Christ, from when, having reached the use of reason, we began to know, with the lights of faith, the sacred mysteries of redemption? What thoughts, what designs, what goods have we loved? Pleasures, pastimes, pride, vengeance, sensuality, behold the goods that imprisoned the affections of our heart. But, if we have faith, let us change our life and loves; let us love a God who suffered so much for us. Let us remember the sorrows that the Heart of Jesus suffered for us from childhood, and thus we will not be able to love but that Heart, which loved us so much.\n\nPRAYER\nOur Lord, do You want to know how we behaved with You in our life? From the moment we began to have the use of reason we began to despise Your grace and Your love. But better than we You know it and, despite that, You endured us because You love us very much. We fled from You, and You approached calling us. That same love that made You come down from heaven to seek the lost sheep, made You endure us. Jesus, now You seek us and we seek You. We perceive that Your grace assists us; it assists us with the sorrow of our sins, which we hate more than all other evils; it assists us with the desire we have to love You and to please You. Yes our Lord, we want to love You and as much as we can. Certainly we fear for our fragility and weakness contracted because of our sins, but much love is the confidence that Your grace infuses in us, making us hope in Your merits and giving us great encouragement to exclaim: 'I can do all things in him who strengtheneth me.' (Phil. 4:13) If we are weak, You will give us strength against our enemies; if we are sick, we hope that Your blood will be our medicine; if we are sinners, we trust that You will sanctify us. We confess that in the past we cooperated with our ruin because we failed to have recourse to You in dangers. From today on, God and our hope, to You we want to have recourse and from You we hope for all help and all good. We love You above all things and we want to love nothing outside of You. Help us, for pity's sake, by the merit of so many sufferings that from the beginning You suffered for us. Eternal Father, for the love of Jesus Christ, accept that we love You. If we angered You, be appeased upon seeing the tears of the child Jesus, who begs You for us: 'Look on the face of thy Christ.' (Ps. 83:10) We do not deserve graces, but Your innocent Son deserves them, who offers You a life of sorrows so that You may be merciful to us.\nAnd You, Mary, Mary, Merciful Mother, do not cease to intercede for us; You know how much we trust in You, and we know well that You do not abandon those who have recourse to You.",
  "novenaNatalDay6Title": "Sixth Day - December 21",
  "novenaNatalDay6Meditation": "JESUS IN THE WOMB OF MARY\n\nI am counted among them that go down to the pit: I am become as a man without help. (Ps. 87:5)\n\nLet us consider the painful life that Jesus Christ passed in the womb of His Mother. He was free, because He had voluntarily made Himself a prisoner of love, but love deprived Him of the use of liberty and kept Him in chains so tight that He could not move. O great patience of the Savior! Thinking of the sorrows of Our Lord still in the womb of His Mother.\n\nLet us see to what the Son of God is reduced for love of men: He deprives Himself of His liberty and chains Himself to free us from the chains of hell. Much, then, deserves to be recognized with gratitude and love the grace of our liberator and surety, who, not by obligation, but by affection, offered to pay and paid our debts and our penalties, giving His life for them: 'Forget not the kindness of thy surety: for he hath given his life for thee.'\n\nPRAYER\n'Forget not the kindness of thy surety.' Yes, O Jesus, with reason the Prophet warns us not to forget the immense grace You did us. We were debtors and guilty, and You innocent. You, our God, wanted to satisfy for our sins with Your sorrows and with Your death. And then we forget this grace and Your love and we dare to turn our backs on You, as if You were not our Lord, the Lord who loved us so much. But, if in the past we forgot, we do not want, our Redeemer, to forget You in the future. Your sorrows and Your death will be our continual thought, and they will always remind us of the love You had for us. We curse the days when, forgetful of how much You suffered for us, we lamentably abused the freedom You gave us to love You and used it to despise You. That freedom that You gave us, today we consecrate it to You. Free us, O Jesus, from the misfortune of seeing ourselves again separated from You and made slaves of the devil. Bind our souls to Your feet so that we may not separate ourselves from You again. Eternal Father, by the captivity that the Child Jesus suffered in the womb of Mary, free us from the chains of the devil and hell.\nAnd You, Mother of God, help us. Carry us imprisoned and bound to the Son of God. For, since Jesus is Your prisoner, He will do all that You command. Tell Him to forgive us and make us holy. Help us, our Mother, by the grace and honor that Jesus Christ did You by dwelling nine months in Your womb.",
  "novenaNatalDay7Title": "Seventh Day - December 22",
  "novenaNatalDay7Meditation": "THE SORROW THAT THE INGRATITUDE OF MEN CAUSED JESUS CHRIST\n\nHe came unto his own, and his own received him not. (Jn. 1:11)\n\nOne Christmas, St. Francis was walking through the forest and the roads groaning and sighing, and when asked the cause of his sadness, he replied: 'How do you want me not to weep seeing that love is not loved? I see God intoxicated with love for men and men so ungrateful to this God.' If the ingratitude of men so afflicted St. Francis, let us consider how much more it afflicted the Heart of Jesus. As soon as He was conceived in the womb of Mary He saw the cruel correspondence He would receive from men. He had come from heaven to kindle the fire of divine love, and that desire made Him come down to earth and suffer an abyss of sorrows and ignominies: 'I am come to cast fire on the earth; and what will I, but that it be kindled?' (Lk. 12:49) And then He saw the abyss of sins that men would commit despite having been witnesses of so many proofs of His love. That was, said St. Bernardine of Siena, what made Him suffer an infinite sorrow. Even among us, when someone sees himself treated ungratefully by another it is an unbearable sorrow, for ingratitude often afflicts the soul more than another pain the body. What sorrow, then, would it cause Jesus, who was our God, to see that, for our ingratitude, His benefits and His love would be paid with displeasures and injuries? 'And they repaid me evil for good: and hatred for my love.' (Ps. 108:5) And still today Jesus Christ laments: 'I am become a stranger to my brethren,' (Ps. 68:9) for He sees that He is not loved nor known by many, as if He had done them no good nor suffered anything for their love.\n\nO my God, what case do we make, even Christians, of the love of Jesus Christ? One day He appeared to Blessed Henry Suso as a pilgrim begging from door to door, being always put out with injuries. How many are like those of whom Job spoke: 'Who said to God: Depart from us, and looked upon the Almighty as if he could do nothing: whereas he had filled their houses with good things.' (Job 22:17) We, even if in the past we have joined those ingrates, do we want to continue with our ingratitude in the future? No, because He does not deserve it, that amiable Child who came from heaven to suffer and die for us so that we might love Him.\n\nPRAYER\nLord Jesus, who came down from heaven so that we might love You, taking a life full of labor and death on a cross, how could we so many times say to You: 'Depart from us,' we do not want You, O our God, if You were not infinite goodness nor had given Your life to forgive us, we would not dare to ask You forgiveness; but we know that You Yourself want to give us peace: 'Return to me, says the Lord of hosts, and I will return to you.' You Yourself, Jesus, who are the offended, intercede for us. We do not want, then, to offend You once again, distrustful of Your mercy. We repent with all our soul for having despised You, my supreme Good. Deign to receive us into Your grace by the blood shed by You. 'Father, I am no longer worthy to be called your son.' No, our Redeemer and Father, we are not worthy to be Your children, because so many times we renounced Your love; but You make us worthy with Your merits. May the very thought of the patience with which You endured our sins for so many years and of the graces You granted us, after all the injuries we did to You, make us live burning in the flames of Your love. Come, then, Lord, we will not expel You again, come dwell in our poor heart. We love You and want to love You forever, and You inflame us ever more, with the remembrance of the love You had for us.",
  "novenaNatalDay8Title": "Eighth Day - December 23",
  "novenaNatalDay8Meditation": "LOVE OF GOD FOR MEN IN THE BIRTH OF JESUS\n\nFor the grace of God our Saviour hath appeared to all men; instructing us, that, denying ungodliness and worldly desires, we should live soberly, and justly, and godly in this world, looking for the blessed hope and coming of the glory of the great God and our Saviour Jesus Christ. (Tit. 2:11-13)\n\nLet us consider that the saving grace of God that appeared to all men was the most profound love of Jesus Christ for men. That love, although on the part of God it was always identical, was not always equally manifest.\n\nBefore it had been promised in many prophecies and concealed under the veil of many figures. But, in the birth of the Redeemer, it let itself be seen clearly, the eternal Word appearing to men as a child lying on the hay, groaning and trembling with cold, beginning thus to satisfy for the penalties we deserved and making known to us the affection He had for us, sacrificing His life for us: 'In this we have known the charity of God, because he hath laid down his life for us.' (1 Jn. 3:16) The saving grace of God, then, appeared, and it appeared to all men. But why did not all know Him and still today are there so many who, being able, do not know Him? Because 'the light is come into the world, and men loved darkness rather than the light.' (Jn. 3:19) They did not know Him nor do they know Him because they do not want to know Him and love the darkness of sin more than the light of grace. Let us not belong to the number of those unfortunates. If until now we have closed our eyes to the light, thinking little of the love of Jesus Christ, let us seek, until the end of our life, to always have before our eyes the sufferings and death of our Redeemer, to love Him who loved us so much: 'awaiting our blessed hope, the appearing of the glory of our great God and Savior Jesus Christ.'\n\nThus we will be able to trust deeply, according to the divine promises, to attain that paradise that Jesus Christ won for us with His blood. In this first manifestation Jesus Christ comes as a child, poor and despised, born in a stable, covered with poor cloths and reclined on the straw, but in the second appearance He will come upon a throne of majesty: 'and they will see the Son of man coming on the clouds of heaven with power and great glory.' Happy at that hour he who has not hated or despised Him.\n\nPRAYER\nO Holy Child, now we contemplate You on the straw, poor, afflicted, and abandoned; but we know that one day You will come to judge us on a splendid throne, surrounded by angels. Forgive us before judging us. Then You will be a rigorous judge, but now You are our Redeemer and our merciful Father. We were ungrateful, not knowing You for not wanting to know You, and instead of thinking of loving You, considering the love You had for us, we only thought of satisfying our appetite, despising Your grace and Your love. In Your hands we place our soul, which we so often strove to lose, so that You may save it. 'Into thy hand I commit my spirit; thou hast redeemed me, O Lord, faithful God.' In You I deposit my hopes, for You are the one who, to ransom me from hell, gave blood and life. Thou hast redeemed me, O Lord, faithful God. You did not make me die when I was in sin and You waited for me with so much patience so that, entering into myself, I might repent of having offended You, begin to love You and thus You could forgive me and save me. Yes, my Jesus, I want to please You; I repent of all the evil and displeasure I have caused You. Save me by Your mercy and let my salvation be to love You always in this life and for all eternity.\nMy beloved Mother, recommend me to Your Son, make Him see that I am Your servant and that in You I have placed my hope, for He hears You and denies You nothing.",
  "novenaNatalDay9Title": "Ninth Day - December 24",
  "novenaNatalDay9Meditation": "JOURNEY OF ST. JOSEPH AND MARY MOST HOLY TO BETHLEHEM\n\nAnd Joseph also went up from Galilee, out of the city of Nazareth into Judea, to the city of David, which is called Bethlehem, to be enrolled with Mary his espoused wife, who was with child. (Lk. 2:4-5)\n\nGod had decreed that His Son be born not even in Joseph's house, but in a cave, in a stable, in the poorest and most painful way that a child can be born; for that He arranged that Caesar Augustus publish an edict in which He ordered that all go to be enrolled in their native city. Joseph, upon having news of that order, certainly hesitated about leaving or taking with him Mary Most Holy, near to giving birth, since he had no wealth to provide her with a convenient journey, nor did he want, on the other hand, to leave her alone and without support.\n\nMary, however, knew that, as the prophet Micah had announced, the Savior must be born in Bethlehem; therefore, taking the cloths and clothes she had prepared for her Son, she left with Joseph, poorly, in wintertime, about to give birth, to submit herself to the will of God.\n\nLet us unite with them, and through the sorrows and pains of our journey through this life, let us praise God, be grateful to Him, asking Him only that Our Lord Jesus Christ be always with us.\n\nLet us ask Joseph and Mary that by the merit of the sorrows suffered in their journey, they accompany us in the journey we are making to eternity.\n\nPRAYER\nMy beloved Redeemer, accompanied on earth only by Joseph and Mary, on going to Bethlehem, permit me to accompany You also, You came down from heaven to be my companion on earth, and I so many times already abandoned You offending You ungratefully. When I think that, so many times, to follow my cursed inclinations, I separated myself from You, renouncing Your friendship, I would die of sorrow. You came to forgive me; thus, then, forgive me immediately, for with all my soul I repent of having so many times turned my back on You and abandoned You. I propose and hope, with Your grace, not to leave You more nor separate myself more from You. Unite me, bind me with the sweet bonds of Your holy love, my Redeemer and my God.\nMost Holy Mary, I come to accompany you on your journey; do not fail to assist me in the one I am making to eternity. Assist me always and, especially, when I find myself at the end of my life, near the moment on which depends being always with you to love Jesus in paradise, or being always far from you, to hate Jesus in hell. My Queen, save me by your intercession, and let my salvation be to love you, you and Jesus, forever, in time and in eternity. You are my hope; in you I trust.",
