  "novenaSaoJoseTitle": "Novena to Saint Joseph",
  "novenaSaoJoseDesc": "To obtain graces and the protection of St. Joseph, patron of families and Terror of Demons.",
  "novenaSaoJoseOpening": "O glorious Saint Joseph, foster father of Jesus and most chaste spouse of Mary, open your paternal heart to us who have recourse to you with confidence. By the love you bore to the Child God, obtain for us the graces which we humbly ask of you. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoJoseClosing": "Glorious Saint Joseph, who were exalted by the Eternal Father, obeyed by the Incarnate Word, favored by the Holy Spirit, and loved by the Virgin Mary; I praise and bless the Most Holy Trinity for the privileges and merits with which it has enriched you. You are most powerful, and never has it been heard that anyone had recourse to you and was left forsaken by you. You are the comforter of the afflicted, the refuge of the needy, and the advocate of sinners. Receive, then, with paternal goodness one who invokes you with filial trust, and obtain for me the graces which I ask of you in this novena. I choose you as my special protector. Be, after Jesus and Mary, my consolation on this earth, my refuge in misfortunes, my guide in uncertainties, my comfort in tribulations, and my solicitous father in all necessities. Obtain for me, finally, as the crown of your favors, a good and holy death in the grace of Our Lord. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoJosePrayers": "Pray 1 Our Father, 1 Hail Mary, and 1 Glory Be.",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay1Title": "Day 1 - Saint Joseph, Foster Father of Jesus",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay1Meditation": "Most lovable Saint Joseph, who had the honor of nourishing, bringing up, and embracing the Messiah, whom so many prophets and kings desired to see and saw not, obtain for me, together with the pardon of my faults, the grace of humble and trusting prayer which obtains all things from God. Receive with paternal goodness the petitions which I make to you in this novena and present them to Jesus, who deigned to obey you upon earth. Amen.\n\nV/. Pray for us, Saint Joseph, foster father of Jesus.\nR/. That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.\n\nLet us pray. O God, who by Thine ineffable Providence didst vouchsafe to choose blessed Joseph to be the Spouse of Thy most holy Mother, grant, we beseech Thee, that he whom we venerate as a protector on earth may deserve to be our intercessor in heaven. Who livest and reignest world without end. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay2Title": "Day 2 - Saint Joseph, Spouse of the Virgin Mary",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay2Meditation": "Saint Joseph, most chaste Spouse of the Mother of God and faithful guardian of her virginity, obtain for me, through Mary, purity of body and soul and victory in all temptations and difficulties. I also commend to you Christian spouses, that united in sincere love and strengthened by grace, they may sustain one another in the sufferings and trials of life. Amen.\n\nV/. Pray for us, Saint Joseph, spouse of the Mother of God.\nR/. That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.\n\nLet us pray. O God, who by Thine ineffable Providence didst vouchsafe to choose blessed Joseph to be the Spouse of Thy most holy Mother, grant, we beseech Thee, that he whom we venerate as a protector on earth may deserve to be our intercessor in heaven. Who livest and reignest world without end. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay3Title": "Day 3 - Saint Joseph, Head of the Holy Family",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay3Meditation": "Glorious Saint Joseph, who enjoyed for so many years the presence and filial affection of Jesus, whom you had the happiness of feeding and clothing together with your Most Holy Spouse, I beseech you to obtain for me the ineffable gift of ever living in union with God by sanctifying grace. Obtain also for Christian parents the grace to fulfill faithfully their grave duties as educators, and for children respect and obedience after the example of the Child Jesus. Amen.\n\nV/. Pray for us, Saint Joseph, head of the Holy Family.\nR/. That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.\n\nLet us pray. O God, who by Thine ineffable Providence didst vouchsafe to choose blessed Joseph to be the Spouse of Thy most holy Mother, grant, we beseech Thee, that he whom we venerate as a protector on earth may deserve to be our intercessor in heaven. Who livest and reignest world without end. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay4Title": "Day 4 - Saint Joseph, Example of Fidelity",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay4Meditation": "Most faithful Saint Joseph, who gave us so fair an example in the faithful fulfillment of your duties as protector of the Most Holy Virgin and foster father of the Redeemer, I beg you to obtain for me the grace to imitate your example in fidelity to all the duties of my state of life. Help me to be faithful in little things, that I may be faithful also in great ones. Obtain this same grace for all who are dear to me in this life, that we may attain in heaven the reward promised to those who are faithful unto death. Amen.\n\nV/. Pray for us, Saint Joseph, example of fidelity.\nR/. That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.\n\nLet us pray. O God, who by Thine ineffable Providence didst vouchsafe to choose blessed Joseph to be the Spouse of Thy most holy Mother, grant, we beseech Thee, that he whom we venerate as a protector on earth may deserve to be our intercessor in heaven. Who livest and reignest world without end. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay5Title": "Day 5 - Saint Joseph, Mirror of Patience",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay5Meditation": "Kind Saint Joseph, who bore with heroic patience the trials and adversities on the journey to Bethlehem, in the flight into Egypt, and during the hidden life at Nazareth, and gave us the example of admirable conformity to the will of God, obtain for me the virtue of patience in the difficulties of each day. Obtain also unconquerable patience for all who bear heavy crosses, that they may be ever more united to Jesus, the divine model of meekness and patience. Amen.\n\nV/. Pray for us, Saint Joseph, mirror of patience.\nR/. That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.\n\nLet us pray. O God, who by Thine ineffable Providence didst vouchsafe to choose blessed Joseph to be the Spouse of Thy most holy Mother, grant, we beseech Thee, that he whom we venerate as a protector on earth may deserve to be our intercessor in heaven. Who livest and reignest world without end. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay6Title": "Day 6 - Saint Joseph, Model of Workers",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay6Meditation": "Humble Saint Joseph, who living in poverty dignified your trade by constant labor and counted yourself happy to serve Jesus and Mary with the fruit of your toil, obtain for me a love for the work imposed upon me as a duty of my state, seeking always to fulfill therein the will of God. Protect the homes of workers against the harmful influences of the enemies of Christ and Holy Church. Obtain for them the grace to sanctify their labor by a right intention, in all things conformed to the designs of Divine Providence. Amen.\n\nV/. Pray for us, Saint Joseph, model of workers.\nR/. That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.\n\nLet us pray. O God, who by Thine ineffable Providence didst vouchsafe to choose blessed Joseph to be the Spouse of Thy most holy Mother, grant, we beseech Thee, that he whom we venerate as a protector on earth may deserve to be our intercessor in heaven. Who livest and reignest world without end. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay7Title": "Day 7 - Saint Joseph, Protector of the Holy Church",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay7Meditation": "Glorious Patriarch Saint Joseph, Protector and Patron of the Universal Church, obtain for me the grace to love the Church as my Mother and to honor her as a true disciple of Christ. I pray you to watch over her Mystical Body, as once you watched over Jesus and Mary. Protect the Holy Father and the Bishops, the Priests and the Religious. Obtain for them holiness of life and fruitfulness in the apostolate. Guard the innocence of childhood, the chastity of youth, the uprightness of the home, and the order and peace of society. Amen.\n\nV/. Pray for us, Saint Joseph, protector of the Holy Church.\nR/. That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.\n\nLet us pray. O God, who by Thine ineffable Providence didst vouchsafe to choose blessed Joseph to be the Spouse of Thy most holy Mother, grant, we beseech Thee, that he whom we venerate as a protector on earth may deserve to be our intercessor in heaven. Who livest and reignest world without end. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay8Title": "Day 8 - Saint Joseph, Comfort of the Sick",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay8Meditation": "Compassionate Saint Joseph, hope of the sick and the needy, aid me in all infirmities and tribulations, obtaining for me full conformity to the admirable designs of God. Obtain also for me, and for all for whom I pray in this novena, the healing of spiritual infirmities, which are inordinate passions, weaknesses, faults, and sins, and protect us against the temptations of the enemy of our salvation. Amen.\n\nV/. Pray for us, Saint Joseph, comfort of the sick.\nR/. That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.\n\nLet us pray. O God, who by Thine ineffable Providence didst vouchsafe to choose blessed Joseph to be the Spouse of Thy most holy Mother, grant, we beseech Thee, that he whom we venerate as a protector on earth may deserve to be our intercessor in heaven. Who livest and reignest world without end. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay9Title": "Day 9 - Saint Joseph, Patron of the Dying",
  "novenaSaoJoseDay9Meditation": "Blessed Saint Joseph, who dying in the arms of Jesus and Mary departed this world adorned with virtues and enriched with merits, assist me in the supreme and decisive hour of my life against the assaults of the infernal powers. Obtain for me the grace to die comforted by the holy Sacraments necessary for my salvation. Have compassion on all the agonizing, obtaining for them the grace of salvation through Mary, your Most Holy Spouse. Amen.\n\nV/. Pray for us, Saint Joseph, patron of the dying.\nR/. That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.\n\nLet us pray. O God, who by Thine ineffable Providence didst vouchsafe to choose blessed Joseph to be the Spouse of Thy most holy Mother, grant, we beseech Thee, that he whom we venerate as a protector on earth may deserve to be our intercessor in heaven. Who livest and reignest world without end. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoJudasTitle": "Novena to Saint Jude Thaddeus",
  "novenaSaoJudasDesc": "To afflicted hearts and desperate cases, we turn to the glorious Saint Jude.",
  "novenaSaoJudasOpening": "O most holy Apostle, St. Jude, faithful servant and friend of Jesus, the Church honors and invokes you universally, as the patron of hopeless cases, of things almost despaired of. Pray for me, I am so helpless and alone. Make use I implore you, of that particular privilege given to you, to bring visible and speedy help where help is almost despaired of. Come to my assistance in this great need that I may receive the consolation and help of heaven in all my necessities, tribulations, and sufferings, particularly (make your request).",
  "novenaSaoJudasClosing": "Final Prayer: Saint Jude Thaddeus, pray for us and for all who invoke your aid! I promise, O blessed St. Jude, to be ever mindful of this great favor, to always honor you as my special and powerful patron, and to gratefully encourage devotion to you. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoJudasPrayers": "Pray 3 Our Fathers, 3 Hail Marys, and 3 Glory Bes.",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay1Title": "Day 1 - Unconditional Fidelity",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay1Meditation": "Saint Jude, valiant witness, I ask for the grace to remain faithful to my faith despite dark times, and the strength never to lose hope in Christ's promises.",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay2Title": "Day 2 - Love of the Cross",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay2Meditation": "Glorious apostle, help me embrace my daily cross with the same joy and readiness with which you laid down your life for the Gospel.",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay3Title": "Day 3 - Purity of Intentions",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay3Meditation": "Beloved Saint Jude, purify my worldly desires so I may seek first to please God, loving my neighbor as myself.",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay4Title": "Day 4 - Peace in Despair",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay4Meditation": "O Patron of the afflicted, let serene peace and full trust in Divine Providence descend upon my troubled heart.",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay5Title": "Day 5 - Salvation of Souls",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay5Meditation": "Inspired by your zeal, St. Jude, I pray to be an instrument of the Lord for the salvation and sanctification of my family.",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay6Title": "Day 6 - The Virtue of Patience",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay6Meditation": "In the contradictions of the journey, O valiant Saint, grant me the patience to endure all in expiation of my own faults.",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay7Title": "Day 7 - Defense of the True Faith",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay7Meditation": "You, St. Jude, who condemned sects and heresies in your Epistle, obtain for me the grace to vigorously defend the Catholic Doctrine.",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay8Title": "Day 8 - Infallible Help",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay8Meditation": "In problems without an apparent solution, I place my trust in your intercession. The Lord will never deny your request, for you gave your blood for Him.",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay9Title": "Day 9 - Eternal Glory",
  "novenaSaoJudasDay9Meditation": "Victorious Saint Jude, guide my steps on the summit of this exiled life, so that, meriting pardon through your assistance, I may bless God with you eternally.",
  "novenaPentecostesTitle": "Novena of Pentecost",
  "novenaPentecostesDesc": "The first novena of the Church, praying for the gifts of the Holy Spirit, like Mary and the Apostles in the Upper Room.",
  "novenaPentecostesOpening": "Come, Holy Spirit! Fill the hearts of Your faithful, and enkindle in them the fire of Your love. Send forth Your Spirit, and they shall be created; and You shall renew the face of the earth. O God, who by the light of the Holy Spirit, did instruct the hearts of the faithful, grant that by the same Holy Spirit we may be truly wise and ever enjoy His consolations. Through Christ Our Lord. Amen.",
  "novenaPentecostesClosing": "Divine Holy Spirit, grant me Your graces and Your seven gifts. May the flame of Your Divine Love purify and sanctify my heart, making it a templar worthy of Your perpetual dwelling. Amen.",
  "novenaPentecostesPrayers": "Pray 1 Our Father, 1 Hail Mary, and the Veni Creator Spiritus (or 1 Glory Be).",
  "novenaPentecostesDay1Title": "Day 1 - Come, Holy Spirit from Heaven",
  "novenaPentecostesDay1Meditation": "The Holy Spirit is the promise of the Father and the light of our soul. Let us ask the Spirit of Truth to descend and kindle our lukewarm faith.",
  "novenaPentecostesDay2Title": "Day 2 - The Gift of the Fear of the Lord",
  "novenaPentecostesDay2Meditation": "Holy Spirit, grant me the holy fear of offending God, delivering me from disrespect and attachment to sin.",
  "novenaPentecostesDay3Title": "Day 3 - The Gift of Piety",
  "novenaPentecostesDay3Meditation": "Lord, flood me with tender affection for You, that I may call You Father and joyfully serve my brothers and sisters.",
  "novenaPentecostesDay4Title": "Day 4 - The Gift of Knowledge",
  "novenaPentecostesDay4Meditation": "Divine Master, grant me the true wisdom of created things, so I am not deceived by the world and may seek the eternal.",
  "novenaPentecostesDay5Title": "Day 5 - The Gift of Fortitude",
  "novenaPentecostesDay5Meditation": "Comforting Spirit, fortify my spirit against fear and temptations. Give me the strength of the martyrs to witness to Christ.",
  "novenaPentecostesDay6Title": "Day 6 - The Gift of Counsel",
  "novenaPentecostesDay6Meditation": "Illuminator of souls, guide my decisions. In the hesitations of life, grant me to choose only what is of Your most holy will.",
  "novenaPentecostesDay7Title": "Day 7 - The Gift of Understanding",
  "novenaPentecostesDay7Meditation": "Divine Light, open my intellect to the revealed truths of faith, and chase away the blindness and ignorance of my mind.",
  "novenaPentecostesDay8Title": "Day 8 - The Gift of Wisdom",
  "novenaPentecostesDay8Meditation": "Sacred Fire of Love, may this gift make me taste the beauty of God, uniting me ever more deeply in true communion with Christ.",
  "novenaPentecostesDay9Title": "Day 9 - The Fruits of the Spirit",
  "novenaPentecostesDay9Meditation": "Beside the Virgin in the Cenacle, I completely open my heart. Form in me charity, joy, peace, and all virtues.",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroTitle": "Novena to Our Lady of Perpetual Help",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDesc": "In all afflictions, the Immaculate Mother never denies Her perpetual aid and mercy.",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroOpening": "O Mother of Perpetual Help, grant that I may ever invoke thy most powerful name, which is the safeguard of the living and the salvation of the dying. O Purest Mary, O Sweetest Mary, let thy name henceforth be ever on my lips. Delay not, O Blessed Lady, to help me whenever I call on thee, for, in all my needs, in all my temptations I shall never cease to call on thee, ever repeating thy sacred name, Mary, Mary.",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroClosing": "Remember, O most gracious Virgin Mary, that never was it known that anyone who fled to thy protection, implored thy help, or sought thy intercession was left unaided. Inspired by this confidence, I fly unto thee, O Virgin of virgins, my Mother; to thee do I come, before thee I stand, sinful and sorrowful. O Mother of the Word Incarnate, despise not my petitions, but in thy mercy hear and answer me. Amen.",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroPrayers": "Pray 3 Hail Marys, followed by: 'O Mary, conceived without sin, pray for us who have recourse to thee.'",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay1Title": "Day 1 - Our Lady, Queen of Mercy",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay1Meditation": "Mary has her merciful eyes constantly upon me. Her blessed arms never close to my appeals.",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay2Title": "Day 2 - Refuge in Despair",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay2Meditation": "Facing desperate temptations, Immaculate Mother, show me the Child Jesus you carry in your arms, my refuge and salvation.",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay3Title": "Day 3 - Help in Sickness and Affliction",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay3Meditation": "No earthly affliction goes unnoticed by Our Lady. I ask You for bodily relief or strength and resignation to fulfill the divine will.",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay4Title": "Day 4 - Star Amidst the Darkness",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay4Meditation": "In the darkness covering the world today, be my Star. Beloved Mother, do not let false fashions lead me away from the cross.",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay5Title": "Day 5 - Protection and Help of Families",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay5Meditation": "O Perpetual Help, pour out abundant blessings on my home. Keep us in unity, love, and purity of life.",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay6Title": "Day 6 - Refuge of Sinners",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay6Meditation": "I acknowledge myself unworthy and weak. Therefore I ask You: obtain for me the tears of sincere and lasting confession of my faults.",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay7Title": "Day 7 - Comfort in Fading Hours",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay7Meditation": "By the piercing pain You had at the foot of the cross, come comfort the anguish of my heart and calm those who strive and sweat for me.",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay8Title": "Day 8 - Fidelity to the Rosary",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay8Meditation": "Sovereign Lady, engrave in my spirit fidelity and constancy to the daily Holy Rosary, a chain of graces and door of salvation.",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay9Title": "Day 9 - The Hour of Our Death",
  "novenaPerpetuoSocorroDay9Meditation": "O merciful and tender Mother! In the final and definitive battle of my life, come to my aid. Receive me and take my soul in the company of the angels.",
  "novenaSaoMiguelTitle": "Novena to Saint Michael the Archangel",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDesc": "Prince of the Heavenly Host, intercessor and powerful combatant for victory against evil attacks.",
  "novenaSaoMiguelOpening": "Saint Michael the Archangel, defend us in battle; be our protection against the wickedness and snares of the devil. May God rebuke him, we humbly pray; and do thou, O Prince of the Heavenly Host, by the power of God, cast into hell Satan and all the evil spirits who prowl about the world seeking the ruin of souls. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoMiguelClosing": "O glorious Prince of the Heavenly Host, St. Michael the Archangel! By Your cry 'Who is like God?', receive my humble petitions and present them before the throne of the Most High. Amen.",
  "novenaSaoMiguelPrayers": "Pray 1 Our Father, 3 Hail Marys, and the Glory Be.",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay1Title": "Day 1 - Most Faithful Prince",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay1Meditation": "St. Michael, by Your zeal for the glory of God, impel me not to have human respect and to always give due honor to Our Lord.",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay2Title": "Day 2 - Destroyer of Pride",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay2Meditation": "Luminous Archangel, who shattered satanic pride, root out in me everything that is not genuine humility.",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay3Title": "Day 3 - Terror of Satan",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay3Meditation": "O terror of the abyss, chase away with Your drawn sword every demonic insinuation of impurity and despair.",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay4Title": "Day 4 - Defender of the Church",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay4Meditation": "Protect Holy Mother Church, the Supreme Pontiff, clergy, and laity from all visible and invisible enemies who plan to destroy Her.",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay5Title": "Day 5 - Comfort of Souls",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay5Meditation": "Formidable St. Michael, bearer of the scale of divine justice, bring comfort in the extreme hour to the agonizing and afflicted.",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay6Title": "Day 6 - Victor in Spiritual Dangers",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay6Meditation": "Help me in hidden struggles. Break with Your warrior cry the bonds of secret vices and habitual faults in my life.",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay7Title": "Day 7 - Standard of the Servants and Soldiers of Christ",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay7Meditation": "Form me into a true valorous disciple of the doctrine, not yielding space or condescension to the deceitful things of the world.",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay8Title": "Day 8 - Shield of Families",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay8Meditation": "Daign St. Michael to place your angels under the door of my home, defending my family from discord and envy.",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay9Title": "Day 9 - Presenter of Souls",
  "novenaSaoMiguelDay9Meditation": "On the day of judgment, when my soul appears before the rigor of the divine scale, I ask that You appear for me as a guarantor. Amen.",
  "novenaAlmasTitle": "Novena for the Holy Souls in Purgatory",
  "novenaAlmasDesc": "The noblest work of charity: interceding through sacrifice to shorten the suffering of the suffering souls.",
  "novenaAlmasOpening": "O Lord Jesus Christ, our Redeemer, who deigned to shed Your most precious Blood to redeem the world and save souls, I humbly beseech You, by the sorrows of Your Most Blessed Mother and Your Divine Wounds, have mercy on the Souls in Purgatory, especially those for whom I am most bound to pray.",
  "novenaAlmasClosing": "Eternal rest grant unto them, O Lord. And let perpetual light shine upon them. May they rest in peace. Amen. Sweet Heart of Mary, be the salvation of the souls in purgatory.",
  "novenaAlmasPrayers": "Pray 1 Our Father, 1 Hail Mary, and the prayer 'Eternal rest grant unto them, O Lord'.",
  "novenaAlmasDay1Title": "Day 1 - The Gravity of Sin",
  "novenaAlmasDay1Meditation": "Souls suffer incredible torments because sin offends a God of infinite goodness. Lord, deliver the forgotten souls and make me weep for my own sins.",
  "novenaAlmasDay2Title": "Day 2 - Parents and Relatives in Purgatory",
  "novenaAlmasDay2Meditation": "Beloved Jesus, I pray for all the souls to whom my family owes blood or debt. Be Their immediate liberation and eternal purification.",
  "novenaAlmasDay3Title": "Day 3 - Souls and Devotions to the Virgin",
  "novenaAlmasDay3Meditation": "Descend, Lady and Heavenly Mother, to the abyss of those sorrows. Relieve the devotees of Your rosary and scapular with the dew of Your merits.",
  "novenaAlmasDay4Title": "Day 4 - The Most Forgotten Soul",
  "novenaAlmasDay4Meditation": "O Mercy of God, I apply this intention for that soul in purgatory who has absolutely NO ONE in the whole world to pray for them.",
  "novenaAlmasDay5Title": "Day 5 - Priests and Religious",
  "novenaAlmasDay5Meditation": "Remembering the great responsibility of the Holy Oils, I pray especially for the priestly souls who delay ascending to Your heavenly vision.",
  "novenaAlmasDay6Title": "Day 6 - The Justice of God",
  "novenaAlmasDay6Meditation": "God's holiness is a consuming fire, demanding payment for the slightest faulty steps. By the merits of the Holy Cross, You pay the debt, Lord Jesus.",
  "novenaAlmasDay7Title": "Day 7 - Those Who Will Be There Longest",
  "novenaAlmasDay7Meditation": "Those souls guilty of the worst purifying pains rely on an infinite intercessor. I ask, O Blood of Christ, erase the endless account.",
  "novenaAlmasDay8Title": "Day 8 - Souls Closest to Heaven",
  "novenaAlmasDay8Meditation": "I cry out for those souls who are at the door, needing that last drop of prayer to enter. May they ascend today to glory!",
  "novenaAlmasDay9Title": "Day 9 - The Holy Sacrifice of the Mass",
  "novenaAlmasDay9Meditation": "Lord, You who on an altar offered everything, unite tomorrow the merits of the Holy Mass to all these souls, rescuing the legions to the heavenly choirs. Amen.",
