  "novenaAparecidaTitle": "Novena to Our Lady of Aparecida",
  "novenaAparecidaDesc": "Patroness of Brazil. Feast on October 12. Nine days at the feet of the Mother whom the people found in the waters of the Paraíba River.",
  "novenaAparecidaOpening": "O Immaculate Virgin, Mother of God and my Mother, Our Lady of Aparecida, Queen and Patroness of Brazil, I place myself under your mantle. Receive my petitions and my thanks and carry them to your Son, Jesus Christ, my Lord and Savior.",
  "novenaAparecidaClosing": "Our Lady of Aparecida, Mother of the Redeemer, bless Brazil, our families and all who turn to you. Show us Jesus and lead us to Him. Amen.",
  "novenaAparecidaPrayers": "Pray 1 Our Father, 3 Hail Marys and the Hail Holy Queen.",
  "novenaAparecidaDay1Title": "Day 1 - The Mother who welcomes us",
  "novenaAparecidaDay1Meditation": "Mother Aparecida, who let yourself be found by the simple, teach me to seek God in humility and to trust in your motherly love.",
  "novenaAparecidaDay2Title": "Day 2 - The net that was filled",
  "novenaAparecidaDay2Meditation": "Like the fishermen who cast their net and filled it, help me trust in the word of Jesus and cast my net again, even after nights without fruit.",
  "novenaAparecidaDay3Title": "Day 3 - Mother of God",
  "novenaAparecidaDay3Meditation": "Holy Mary, Mother of God, who said yes to the angel, give me a heart willing to do the Lord's will in everything.",
  "novenaAparecidaDay4Title": "Day 4 - Mother of the poor and afflicted",
  "novenaAparecidaDay4Meditation": "Mother Aparecida, look upon those who go hungry, who have no home or work, and make me attentive to the needs of those near me.",
  "novenaAparecidaDay5Title": "Day 5 - Mother of the Church",
  "novenaAparecidaDay5Meditation": "Protect the Holy Church, the Pope, the bishops, the priests and all the faithful. Make us one people, united around Jesus.",
  "novenaAparecidaDay6Title": "Day 6 - Mother of families",
  "novenaAparecidaDay6Meditation": "Keep our families from selfishness and discord. May prayer, forgiveness and the peace of Nazareth reign in every home.",
  "novenaAparecidaDay7Title": "Day 7 - Refuge of sinners",
  "novenaAparecidaDay7Meditation": "Mother of mercy, lead me to confession and sincere conversion. Free me from sin and strengthen my desire to begin again.",
  "novenaAparecidaDay8Title": "Day 8 - Health of the sick",
  "novenaAparecidaDay8Meditation": "Care for the sick and for those who care for them. Give them relief and hope, and give me the grace to visit and console them.",
  "novenaAparecidaDay9Title": "Day 9 - Patroness of Brazil",
  "novenaAparecidaDay9Meditation": "Mother and Queen of Brazil, I consecrate to you my life and my country. May your people live faith, justice and brotherhood. Amen.",
  "novenaFatimaTitle": "Novena to Our Lady of Fátima",
  "novenaFatimaDesc": "Feast on May 13. The message of Fátima: prayer, penance, reparation and the Rosary every day.",
  "novenaFatimaOpening": "O Virgin of Fátima, Mother of Heaven, who came into the world to ask for prayer, penance and conversion, receive this novena which I make with trust. Teach me to pray the rosary every day and to offer my sacrifices to God for the salvation of souls.",
  "novenaFatimaClosing": "O my Jesus, forgive us our sins, save us from the fires of hell, lead all souls to Heaven, especially those most in need of Thy mercy. Our Lady of the Rosary of Fátima, pray for us. Amen.",
  "novenaFatimaPrayers": "Pray the rosary (or at least one decade) and the prayer: \"O my Jesus, forgive us\".",
  "novenaFatimaDay1Title": "Day 1 - Pray the rosary every day",
  "novenaFatimaDay1Meditation": "Our Lady asked that we pray the rosary daily. Give me perseverance to be faithful to this meeting with the Mother and her Son.",
  "novenaFatimaDay2Title": "Day 2 - Penance",
  "novenaFatimaDay2Meditation": "Teach me to accept the small crosses of each day with love and to offer them to God in reparation for sins.",
  "novenaFatimaDay3Title": "Day 3 - Reparation",
  "novenaFatimaDay3Meditation": "O Mother, I want to console the Heart of Jesus and yours, so greatly offended. Accept my prayer as reparation for the sins of the world.",
  "novenaFatimaDay4Title": "Day 4 - The conversion of sinners",
  "novenaFatimaDay4Meditation": "Pray for me and for all sinners. May no one be lost, and may each return to the arms of the Father.",
  "novenaFatimaDay5Title": "Day 5 - Peace in the world",
  "novenaFatimaDay5Meditation": "Mother of Peace, drive away wars and hatred. Make me an instrument of peace in the places where I live.",
  "novenaFatimaDay6Title": "Day 6 - The example of the shepherd children",
  "novenaFatimaDay6Meditation": "Francisco, Jacinta and Lúcia, teach me the simplicity, courage and spirit of sacrifice with which you answered the Lady's request.",
  "novenaFatimaDay7Title": "Day 7 - The Immaculate Heart of Mary",
  "novenaFatimaDay7Meditation": "Immaculate Heart of Mary, be my refuge and the way that leads me to God. In you I want to find shelter and strength.",
  "novenaFatimaDay8Title": "Day 8 - Reparative communion",
  "novenaFatimaDay8Meditation": "I want to approach the sacraments with faith: to confess, receive Communion and pray the rosary on the First Saturdays, as you asked.",
  "novenaFatimaDay9Title": "Day 9 - The consecration",
  "novenaFatimaDay9Meditation": "Mother of Heaven, I consecrate to you my life, my family and the whole world. May your Immaculate Heart triumph. Amen.",
  "novenaMisericordiaTitle": "Divine Mercy Novena",
  "novenaMisericordiaDesc": "Begins on Good Friday and ends on the Saturday before Divine Mercy Sunday. Each day, an intention asked by Jesus of Saint Faustina.",
  "novenaMisericordiaOpening": "Jesus, I trust in You! Fountain of mercy, I bring to this novena the souls You ask me to bring to Your Heart. May the blood and water that flowed from Your side be the refuge of all mankind.",
  "novenaMisericordiaClosing": "Eternal Father, look with mercy upon the souls I have presented to You and, through the merits of the sorrowful Passion of Your Son, pour out Your grace upon them. Jesus, I trust in You! Amen.",
  "novenaMisericordiaPrayers": "Pray the Chaplet of Divine Mercy for the intention of the day.",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay1Title": "Day 1 - All mankind, especially sinners",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay1Meditation": "Merciful Jesus, I bring You all people, especially sinners. Plunge them into the ocean of Your mercy.",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay2Title": "Day 2 - Priests and religious",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay2Meditation": "I bring You priests and consecrated souls. Give them strength to be faithful and to carry the light of Your mercy to others.",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay3Title": "Day 3 - Devout and faithful souls",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay3Meditation": "I bring You devout and faithful souls. Strengthen them in their trials and help them grow in Your love.",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay4Title": "Day 4 - Those who do not yet know Jesus",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay4Meditation": "I bring You those who do not yet know You. May the light of Your Heart shine on them and draw them to You.",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay5Title": "Day 5 - Those who have left the Church",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay5Meditation": "I bring You those who have separated from the unity of the Church. Lead them back to communion, that all may be one.",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay6Title": "Day 6 - The meek, the humble and children",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay6Meditation": "I bring You meek and humble souls and children. May they find rest in Your Heart.",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay7Title": "Day 7 - Those who venerate His Mercy",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay7Meditation": "I bring You the souls who venerate and glorify Your mercy. May they be apostles of trust in You.",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay8Title": "Day 8 - The souls in Purgatory",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay8Meditation": "I bring You the souls in Purgatory. May the blood and water from Your side refresh them and bring them to the joy of Heaven.",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay9Title": "Day 9 - Lukewarm souls",
  "novenaMisericordiaDay9Meditation": "I bring You lukewarm and cold souls. Rekindle in them the fire of Your love and give them the grace to begin again. Amen.",
  "novenaSantoAntonioTitle": "Novena to Saint Anthony",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDesc": "Feast on June 13. Doctor of the Church, preacher of the Gospel and friend of the poor, invoked by those who seek what they have lost.",
  "novenaSantoAntonioOpening": "Glorious Saint Anthony, doctor of the Gospel and friend of the poor, whom God filled with wisdom and kindness, hear my petitions. Help me find what I lack and, above all, always find Jesus.",
  "novenaSantoAntonioClosing": "Saint Anthony, powerful intercessor, present our needs to God. Grant that, through your intercession, we may find what we have lost and, above all, never lose the grace of God. Amen.",
  "novenaSantoAntonioPrayers": "Pray 1 Our Father, 1 Hail Mary and 1 Glory Be, and the Responsory of Saint Anthony, if you wish.",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay1Title": "Day 1 - Preacher of the Gospel",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay1Meditation": "Saint Anthony, who proclaimed the Word with your life and your lips, give me the desire to know and live the Gospel.",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay2Title": "Day 2 - Doctor of the Church",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay2Meditation": "Wise teacher of Scripture, teach me to unite faith and intelligence and to defend the truth with humility and charity.",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay3Title": "Day 3 - Friend of the poor",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay3Meditation": "You who shared what you had, open my heart to the needy and free me from attachment to money.",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay4Title": "Day 4 - Model of humility",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay4Meditation": "Saint Anthony, who chose the last place, free me from pride and vanity and teach me to serve without seeking recognition.",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay5Title": "Day 5 - Wonder-worker",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay5Meditation": "Saint of miracles, through whom God worked wonders, strengthen my faith in the Lord's promises.",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay6Title": "Day 6 - Protector of what is lost",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay6Meditation": "Help me find lost things, and also the peace, direction and faith I may have lost along the way.",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay7Title": "Day 7 - Protector of families",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay7Meditation": "Bless couples, engaged persons and families. May they live united in love and faithfulness to God.",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay8Title": "Day 8 - Devoted to the Eucharist",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay8Meditation": "Saint Anthony, who adored Jesus in the Blessed Sacrament, teach me to love the Eucharist and to receive it with faith.",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay9Title": "Day 9 - Intercessor before God",
  "novenaSantoAntonioDay9Meditation": "Bring my petitions to the Lord and give me confidence in your help. May I obtain the grace I need and the Heaven I hope for. Amen.",
  "novenaSantaRitaTitle": "Novena to Saint Rita of Cascia",
  "novenaSantaRitaDesc": "Feast on May 22. Wife, mother, widow and religious, invoked in difficult and desperate causes.",
  "novenaSantaRitaOpening": "Saint Rita, advocate of impossible causes, who spent your whole life united to Christ crucified, hear my petition. Obtain for me from God the grace I need, if it is for His glory and the good of my soul.",
  "novenaSantaRitaClosing": "Saint Rita of Cascia, woman of prayer and forgiveness, pray for us. Obtain for us patience in our crosses, peace in our families, and the grace to trust in God when all seems lost. Amen.",
  "novenaSantaRitaPrayers": "Pray 1 Our Father, 3 Hail Marys and 1 Glory Be.",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay1Title": "Day 1 - Patient wife",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay1Meditation": "Saint Rita, who patiently endured a difficult marriage, give me peace and strength in the trials of family life.",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay2Title": "Day 2 - Devoted mother",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay2Meditation": "Pray for all mothers and for their children. May I know how to educate in the faith, with love and firmness.",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay3Title": "Day 3 - Woman of forgiveness",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay3Meditation": "You who forgave the murderers of your husband, teach me to forgive from the heart those who have hurt me.",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay4Title": "Day 4 - Trusting widow",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay4Meditation": "Console those who mourn the loss of a loved one and those who live in loneliness. May they find their hope in God.",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay5Title": "Day 5 - Obedient religious",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay5Meditation": "Saint Rita, who overcame difficulties to consecrate your life to God, help me persevere in what the Lord asks of me.",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay6Title": "Day 6 - Lover of Christ's Passion",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay6Meditation": "You who received on your forehead a thorn of the Lord, help me understand the value of suffering united to the cross of Jesus.",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay7Title": "Day 7 - Peacemaker",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay7Meditation": "Saint Rita, who reconciled enemies, bring peace to divided families and hardened hearts.",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay8Title": "Day 8 - Advocate of impossible causes",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay8Meditation": "Intercede for this cause that seems to have no way out. Obtain for me the grace, or the strength to accept God's will.",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay9Title": "Day 9 - Consolation of the sick",
  "novenaSantaRitaDay9Meditation": "Saint Rita, help the sick and those who suffer in body and soul. May I always trust in the goodness of the Lord. Amen.",
  "novenaCristoReiTitle": "Novena to Christ the King",
  "novenaCristoReiDesc": "Solemnity of Our Lord Jesus Christ, King of the Universe, on the last Sunday of Ordinary Time. Nine days to ask that Christ reign in our lives.",
  "novenaCristoReiOpening": "Lord Jesus Christ, King of the Universe, I place myself before You to acknowledge You as my Lord and my King. Come and reign in my heart, in my family and in all of society.",
  "novenaCristoReiClosing": "Christ the King, Prince of Peace, may Your Kingdom of truth, justice, love and peace come to us. Reign in our hearts, in our homes and in our nations, now and forever. Amen.",
  "novenaCristoReiPrayers": "Pray 1 Our Father, 1 Hail Mary and 1 Glory Be, and the Litany of the Sacred Heart, if you wish.",
  "novenaCristoReiDay1Title": "Day 1 - King of the Universe",
  "novenaCristoReiDay1Meditation": "Lord Jesus, through You all things were created. Teach me to acknowledge Your sovereignty over the world and over my life.",
  "novenaCristoReiDay2Title": "Day 2 - King of Truth",
  "novenaCristoReiDay2Meditation": "You came to bear witness to the truth. Give me the grace to live in the truth and never be ashamed of the Gospel.",
  "novenaCristoReiDay3Title": "Day 3 - King of Peace",
  "novenaCristoReiDay3Meditation": "Prince of Peace, disarm my heart and the nations. Make me a builder of the peace that only You can give.",
  "novenaCristoReiDay4Title": "Day 4 - King of Mercy",
  "novenaCristoReiDay4Meditation": "King who forgives, welcome me when I fall. May I receive Your forgiveness and bring it to my brothers and sisters.",
  "novenaCristoReiDay5Title": "Day 5 - King of Hearts",
  "novenaCristoReiDay5Meditation": "Reign in my thoughts, desires and affections. May nothing in me be contrary to Your will.",
  "novenaCristoReiDay6Title": "Day 6 - King of Families",
  "novenaCristoReiDay6Meditation": "May Your kingdom of love be established in our homes. May prayer and forgiveness be the foundation of every family.",
  "novenaCristoReiDay7Title": "Day 7 - King of Nations",
  "novenaCristoReiDay7Meditation": "Enlighten rulers and peoples. May laws and societies respect the dignity of the person and the common good.",
  "novenaCristoReiDay8Title": "Day 8 - Eucharistic King",
  "novenaCristoReiDay8Meditation": "You reign on the altar and in the tabernacle. Teach me to adore You and receive You with love and reverence.",
  "novenaCristoReiDay9Title": "Day 9 - King of Glory",
  "novenaCristoReiDay9Meditation": "May I one day behold Your glory and reign with You in Heaven. Thy Kingdom come. Amen.",
