  "prayerStFrancisPeaceTitle": "Peace Prayer (Saint Francis)",
  "prayerStFrancisPeaceContent": "Lord, make me an instrument of your peace:\nwhere there is hatred, let me sow love;\nwhere there is injury, pardon;\nwhere there is discord, union;\nwhere there is doubt, faith;\nwhere there is error, truth;\nwhere there is despair, hope;\nwhere there is darkness, light;\nwhere there is sadness, joy.\n\nO Divine Master, grant that I may not so much seek\nto be consoled as to console,\nto be understood as to understand,\nto be loved as to love.\nFor it is in giving that we receive,\nit is in pardoning that we are pardoned,\nand it is in dying that we are born to eternal life.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerStFrancisPeaceContentLatin": "Domine, fac me servum pacis tuae.\nUbi odium est, ibi caritatem afferam;\nubi iniuria, veniam;\nubi discordia, concordiam;\nubi dubium, fidem;\nubi error, veritatem;\nubi desperatio, spem;\nubi tristitia, laetitiam;\nubi tenebrae, lucem.\n\nO Magister, fac ut non quaeram\nconsolari, sed consolare;\nintellegi, sed intellegere;\namari, sed amare.\nQuia dando accipitur,\nignoscendo ignoscitur,\net moriendo ad vitam aeternam resurgitur.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerStBenedictMedalTitle": "Medal of Saint Benedict",
  "prayerStBenedictMedalContent": "May the Holy Cross be my light!\nLet not the dragon be my guide.\nBegone, Satan!\nNever tempt me with your vanities!\nWhat you offer is evil;\nDrink your own poison!\n\nIn the name of the Father, and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerStBenedictMedalContentLatin": "Crux sacra sit mihi lux,\nnon draco sit mihi dux.\nVade retro, Satana!\nNumquam suade mihi vana;\nsunt mala quae libas,\nipse venena bibas.\n\nIn nomine Patris, et Filii, et Spiritus Sancti.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerUniversalClementTitle": "Universal Prayer (Pope Clement XI)",
  "prayerUniversalClementContent": "Lord, I believe in Thee: but let me believe more strongly. I hope in Thee: but let me hope more securely. I love Thee: but let me love Thee more ardently. I sorrow for my sins: but let me sorrow more vehemently.\n\nI adore Thee as my first beginning; I long for Thee as my last end; I praise Thee as my constant benefactor; I call on Thee as my loving protector.\n\nGuide me by Thy wisdom, hold me with Thy justice, comfort me with Thy mercy, protect me with Thy power.\n\nI offer Thee, O Lord, my thoughts, to be fixed on Thee; my words, to be about Thee; my actions, to be according to Thee; my sufferings, to be endured for Thee.\n\nI will whatsoever Thou willest, I will it because Thou willest it, I will it in the way Thou willest it, and for as long as Thou willest it.\n\nI pray, O Lord: enlighten my understanding, inflame my will, purify my heart, sanctify my soul.\n\nMay I not be infected by pride, nor affected by flattery, nor deceived by the world, nor entrapped by Satan.\n\nGrant me grace to cleanse my memory, to bridle my tongue, to restrain my eyes, and to discipline my senses.\n\nMay I weep for my past iniquities, repel future temptations, correct my sinful inclinations, and cultivate fitting virtues.\n\nGrant me, O good God, love of Thee, hatred of myself, zeal for my neighbor, and contempt for the world.\n\nMay I strive to obey my superiors, assist my inferiors, counsel my friends, and envy no one.\n\nMay I remember, O Jesus, Thy command and example: by loving my enemies, suffering injuries, doing good to those who persecute me, and praying for my detractors.\n\nMay I conquer sensuality by austerity, avarice by generosity, anger by mildness, and lukewarmness by piety.\n\nMake me prudent in my counsels, steadfast in dangers, patient in adversities, and humble in prosperities.\n\nGrant, O Lord, that I may be attentive in prayer, sober at meals, diligent in my duties, and firm in my resolutions.\n\nMay I take care to have interior holiness, exterior modesty, exemplary conversation, and a well-ordered life.\n\nMay I watch over myself to subdue nature, foster grace, keep Thy law, and attain salvation.\n\nMay I attain holiness through sincere confession of sins, fervent Communion of the Body of Christ, continual recollection of mind, and pure intention of heart.\n\nMay I learn from Thee, O God, how slight is all that is earthly, how great is all that is divine, how brief is all that is temporal, and how enduring is all that is eternal. Amen.",
  "prayerUniversalClementContentLatin": "Credo, Domine, sed credam firmius; spero, sed sperem securius; amo, sed amem ardentius; doleo, sed doleam vehementius.\n\nAdoro te ut primum principium; desidero ut finem ultimum; laudo ut benefactorem perpetuum; invoco ut defensorem propitium.\n\nTua me sapientia dirige, iustitia contine, clementia solare, potentia protege.\n\nOffero tibi, Domine, cogitanda, ut sint ad te; dicenda, ut sint de te; facienda, ut sint secundum te; ferenda, ut sint propter te.\n\nVolo quidquid vis, volo quia vis, volo quomodo vis, volo quamdiu vis.\n\nOro, Domine: intellectum illumines, voluntatem inflammes, cor emundes, animam sanctifices.\n\nA superbia non inficiar; adulatione non afficiar; a mundo non decipiar; a Satana non circumveniar.\n\nGratiam praesta memoriam purgandi, linguam frenandi, oculos cohibendi, sensus coercendi.\n\nDefleam praeteritas iniquitates, repellam futuras tentationes, corrigam vitiosas propensiones, excolam idoneas virtutes.\n\nTribue mihi, bone Deus, amorem tui, odium mei, zelum proximi, contemptum mundi.\n\nStudeam superioribus oboedire, inferioribus subvenire, amicis consulere, nemini invidere.\n\nMeminerim, o Iesu, mandati tui et exempli, inimicos diligendo, iniurias sufferendo, persequentibus benefaciendo, pro calumniantibus orando.\n\nVincam voluptatem austeritate, avaritiam largitate, iracundiam lenitate, tepiditatem pietate.\n\nRedde me prudentem in consiliis, constantem in periculis, patientem in adversis, humilem in prosperis.\n\nFac, Domine, ut sim in oratione attentus, in epulis sobrius, in munere sedulus, in proposito firmus.\n\nCurem habere sanctitatem interiorem, modestiam exteriorem, conversationem exemplarem, vitam regularem.\n\nNaturae invigilem domandae, gratiae fovendae, legi servandae, saluti promerendae.\n\nSanctimoniam assequar sincera peccatorum confessione, fervida Corporis Christi communione, continua mentis recollectione, pura cordis intentione.\n\nDiscam a te, Deus, quam tenue, quod terrenum; quam grande, quod divinum; quam breve, quod temporaneum; quam durabile, quod aeternum. Amen.",
  "prayerStTeresaAvilaTitle": "Let nothing disturb you (Saint Teresa of Ávila)",
  "prayerStTeresaAvilaContent": "Let nothing disturb you,\nLet nothing frighten you,\nAll things are passing.\nGod never changes.\nPatience obtains all things.\nWhoever has God\nLacks nothing;\nGod alone suffices.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerStTeresaAvilaContentLatin": "Nihil te perturbet,\nnihil te terreat,\nomnia transeunt.\nDeus non mutatur.\nPatientia omnia assequitur.\nQui Deum habet,\nnihil illi deest:\nsolus Deus sufficit.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerStAugustineTitle": "Late have I loved You (Saint Augustine)",
  "prayerStAugustineContent": "Late have I loved You, O Beauty ever ancient, ever new, late have I loved You! You were within me, but I was outside, and it was there that I searched for You. In my unloveliness I plunged into the lovely things which You created. You were with me, but I was not with You. Created things kept me far from You; yet, if they had not been in You, they would not have been at all.\n\nYou called, You shouted, and You broke through my deafness. You flashed, You shone, and You dispelled my blindness. You breathed Your fragrance on me; I drew in breath and now I pant for You. I tasted You, and now I hunger and thirst for You. You touched me, and I burned for Your peace.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerStAugustineContentLatin": "Sero te amavi, pulchritudo tam antiqua et tam nova, sero te amavi! Et ecce intus eras et ego foris, et ibi te quaerebam, et in ista formosa, quae fecisti, deformis irruebam. Mecum eras, et tecum non eram. Ea me tenebant longe a te, quae si in te non essent, non essent.\n\nVocasti et clamasti et rupisti surditatem meam; coruscasti, splenduisti et fugasti caecitatem meam; fragrasti, et duxi spiritum et anhelo tibi; gustavi et esurio et sitio; tetigisti me, et exarsi in pacem tuam.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerStAnthonyTitle": "Prayer to Saint Anthony",
  "prayerStAnthonyContent": "O blessed Saint Anthony, gentlest and kindest of Saints, your love of God and charity for His creatures made you worthy, when on earth, to possess miraculous powers. Encouraged by this thought, I implore you to obtain for me the favor I seek.\n\nO gentle and loving Saint Anthony, whose heart was ever full of human sympathy, whisper my prayer into the ears of the sweet Infant Jesus, who loved to linger in your arms. A whisper from you and my prayer will be granted.\n\nHave pity on me and obtain for me this grace, that my heart may ever give thanks to you, and above all, that I may remain faithful to the commandments of God until the end of my life.\n\nV. Pray for us, blessed Saint Anthony.\nR. That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerStAnthonyContentLatin": "O beate Antoni, sanctorum mitissime, cuius caritas in Deum ac proximum te miraculis clarum fecit in terris. Eadem fiducia recreati, ad te supplices confugimus ut gratiam quam fidenter expetimus impetrare digneris.\n\nO dulcissime Sancte Antoni, cuius pectus misericordia redundabat, affer precem nostram ad aures Divini Infantis Iesu, qui in ulnis tuis requiescere gaudebat. Sufficit enim verbum tuum ut nostra exaudiatur petitio.\n\nMiserere nostri et hanc gratiam impetra, ut gratias tibi semper agamus, et praesertim mandatis Dei usque ad vitae finem fideles maneamus.\n\nV. Ora pro nobis, beate Antoni.\nR. Ut digni efficiamur promissionibus Christi.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerStRitaTitle": "Prayer to Saint Rita of Cascia",
  "prayerStRitaContent": "O powerful and glorious Saint Rita of Cascia, behold at your feet a soul in need, who turns to you with the sweet hope of being heard by you who bear the incomparable title of Saint of the Impossible and Desperate Cases.\n\nO dear Saint, take an interest in my cause, intercede with God to grant me the grace of which I am in so much need. Do not allow me to depart from your feet unheard.\n\nIf there is in me any obstacle which hinders me from obtaining the favor I ask, help me to remove it. Look upon my sufferings and bless my sorrowing heart through your powerful intercession. Trusting in your power with the Sacred Heart of Jesus, I implore your help.\n\nV. Pray for us, Saint Rita, advocate of the impossible.\nR. That we may be made worthy of the promises of Christ.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerStRitaContentLatin": "O potens et gloriosa Sancta Rita, ecce ad pedes tuos afflicta anima, quae ad te confugit spe plena exaudiendi a te, quae Patrona Causarum Impossibilium et Desperatarum merito appellaris.\n\nO dilecta Sancta, suscipe causam meam, intercede pro me apud Deum ut gratiam qua vehementer indigeo consequi merear. Noli me a pedibus tuis vacuum dimittere.\n\nSi quid in me est quod divinae gratiae obstet, adiuva me ut illud expellam. Respice tribulationes meas et consolare cor meum maerens. Fidens potentia tua apud Sacratissimum Cor Iesu, auxilium tuum imploro.\n\nV. Ora pro nobis, Sancta Rita, patrona impossibilium.\nR. Ut digni efficiamur promissionibus Christi.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerLitanyHumilityTitle": "Litany of Humility",
  "prayerLitanyHumilityContent": "O Jesus, meek and humble of heart, hear me.\n\nFrom the desire of being esteemed, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the desire of being loved, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the desire of being extolled, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the desire of being honored, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the desire of being praised, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the desire of being preferred to others, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the desire of being consulted, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the desire of being approved, deliver me, Jesus.\n\nFrom the fear of being humiliated, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the fear of being despised, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the fear of suffering rebukes, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the fear of being calumniated, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the fear of being forgotten, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the fear of being ridiculed, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the fear of being wronged, deliver me, Jesus.\nFrom the fear of being suspected, deliver me, Jesus.\n\nThat others may be loved more than I, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.\nThat others may be esteemed more than I, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.\nThat in the opinion of the world, others may increase and I may decrease, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.\nThat others may be chosen and I set aside, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.\nThat others may be praised and I unnoticed, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.\nThat others may be preferred to me in everything, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.\nThat others may become holier than I, provided that I may become as holy as I should, Jesus, grant me the grace to desire it.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerLitanyHumilityContentLatin": "Iesu, mitis et humilis corde, exaudi me.\n\nA desiderio aestimandi, libera me, Iesu.\nA desiderio amandi, libera me, Iesu.\nA desiderio laudandi, libera me, Iesu.\nA desiderio honorandi, libera me, Iesu.\nA desiderio praeferendi aliis, libera me, Iesu.\nA desiderio consulendi, libera me, Iesu.\nA desiderio approbandi, libera me, Iesu.\n\nA timore humiliandi, libera me, Iesu.\nA timore contemnendi, libera me, Iesu.\nA timore reprehendendi, libera me, Iesu.\nA timore calumniandi, libera me, Iesu.\nA timore oblivioni tradendi, libera me, Iesu.\nA timore irridendi, libera me, Iesu.\nA timore iniuria afficiendi, libera me, Iesu.\nA timore suspecti habendi, libera me, Iesu.\n\nUt alii magis amentur quam ego, Iesu, da mihi gratiam hoc exoptandi.\nUt alii magis aestimentur quam ego, Iesu, da mihi gratiam hoc exoptandi.\nUt alii crescant in existimatione saeculi et ego minuar, Iesu, da mihi gratiam hoc exoptandi.\nUt alii eligantur et ego praeterear, Iesu, da mihi gratiam hoc exoptandi.\nUt alii laudentur et ego negligar, Iesu, da mihi gratiam hoc exoptandi.\nUt alii mihi in omnibus praeferantur, Iesu, da mihi gratiam hoc exoptandi.\nUt alii sanctiores evadant quam ego, dummodo ego tam sanctus fiam quam debeo, Iesu, da mihi gratiam hoc exoptandi.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerLitanyPreciousBloodTitle": "Litany of the Precious Blood",
  "prayerLitanyPreciousBloodContent": "Lord, have mercy on us.\nChrist, have mercy on us.\nLord, have mercy on us.\n\nChrist, hear us.\nChrist, graciously hear us.\n\nGod the Father of Heaven, have mercy on us.\nGod the Son, Redeemer of the world, have mercy on us.\nGod the Holy Spirit, have mercy on us.\nHoly Trinity, One God, have mercy on us.\n\nBlood of Christ, only-begotten Son of the eternal Father, save us.\nBlood of Christ, Incarnate Word of God, save us.\nBlood of Christ, of the New and Eternal Testament, save us.\nBlood of Christ, falling upon the earth in Agony, save us.\nBlood of Christ, shed profusely in the Scourging, save us.\nBlood of Christ, flowing forth in the Crowning with Thorns, save us.\nBlood of Christ, poured out on the Cross, save us.\nBlood of Christ, price of our salvation, save us.\nBlood of Christ, without which there is no forgiveness, save us.\nBlood of Christ, Eucharistic drink and refreshment of souls, save us.\nBlood of Christ, stream of mercy, save us.\nBlood of Christ, victor over demons, save us.\nBlood of Christ, courage of Martyrs, save us.\nBlood of Christ, strength of Confessors, save us.\nBlood of Christ, bringing forth Virgins, save us.\nBlood of Christ, help of those in peril, save us.\nBlood of Christ, relief of the burdened, save us.\nBlood of Christ, solace in sorrow, save us.\nBlood of Christ, hope of the penitent, save us.\nBlood of Christ, consolation of the dying, save us.\nBlood of Christ, peace and tenderness of hearts, save us.\nBlood of Christ, pledge of eternal life, save us.\nBlood of Christ, freeing souls from purgatory, save us.\nBlood of Christ, most worthy of all glory and honor, save us.\n\nLamb of God, who take away the sins of the world, spare us, O Lord.\nLamb of God, who take away the sins of the world, graciously hear us, O Lord.\nLamb of God, who take away the sins of the world, have mercy on us.\n\nV. You have redeemed us, O Lord, in Your Blood.\nR. And made us, for our God, a kingdom.\n\nLet us pray: Almighty and eternal God, You have appointed Your only-begotten Son the Redeemer of the world and willed to be appeased by His Blood. Grant that we may worthily adore this price of our salvation and through its power be safeguarded from the evils of the present life, so that we may rejoice in its fruits forever in heaven. Through Christ our Lord. Amen.",
  "prayerLitanyPreciousBloodContentLatin": "Kyrie, eleison.\nChriste, eleison.\nKyrie, eleison.\n\nChriste, audi nos.\nChriste, exaudi nos.\n\nPater de caelis, Deus, miserere nobis.\nFili, Redemptor mundi, Deus, miserere nobis.\nSpiritus Sancte, Deus, miserere nobis.\nSancta Trinitas, unus Deus, miserere nobis.\n\nSanguis Christi, Unigeniti Patris Aeterni, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, Verbi Dei incarnati, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, Novi et Aeterni Testamenti, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, in agonia decurrens in terram, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, in flagellatione effusus, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, in coronatione spinarum emanans, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, in Cruce effusus, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, pretium nostrae salutis, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, sine quo non fit remissio, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, in Eucharistia potus et lavacrum animarum, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, flumen misericordiae, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, victor daemonum, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, fortitudo martyrum, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, virtus confessorum, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, germinans virgines, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, robur periclitantium, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, levamen laborantium, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, in fletu solatium, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, spes paenitentium, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, solamen morientium, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, pax et dulcedo cordium, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, pignus vitae aeternae, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, animas liberans de lacu Purgatorii, salva nos.\nSanguis Christi, omni honore et gloria dignissimus, salva nos.\n\nAgnus Dei, qui tollis peccata mundi, parce nobis, Domine.\nAgnus Dei, qui tollis peccata mundi, exaudi nos, Domine.\nAgnus Dei, qui tollis peccata mundi, miserere nobis.\n\nV. Redemisti nos, Domine, in sanguine tuo.\nR. Et fecisti nos Deo nostro regnum.\n\nOremus: Omnipotens sempiterne Deus, qui unigenitum Filium tuum mundi Redemptorem constituisti, ac eius sanguine placari voluisti: concede, quaesumus, salutis nostrae pretium ita venerari, atque a praesentis vitae malis eius virtute defendi in terris, ut fructu perpetuo laetemur in caelis. Per eundem Christum Dominum nostrum. Amen.",
  "prayerLitanyBlessedSacramentTitle": "Litany of the Blessed Sacrament",
  "prayerLitanyBlessedSacramentContent": "Lord, have mercy on us.\nChrist, have mercy on us.\nLord, have mercy on us.\n\nChrist, hear us.\nChrist, graciously hear us.\n\nGod the Father of Heaven, have mercy on us.\nGod the Son, Redeemer of the world, have mercy on us.\nGod the Holy Spirit, have mercy on us.\nHoly Trinity, One God, have mercy on us.\n\nLiving Bread that came down from Heaven, have mercy on us.\nHidden God and Savior, have mercy on us.\nWheat of the elect, have mercy on us.\nWine producing virgins, have mercy on us.\nBread of fatness and royal dainties, have mercy on us.\nPerpetual Sacrifice, have mercy on us.\nPure Oblation, have mercy on us.\nLamb without spot, have mercy on us.\nMost pure Banquet, have mercy on us.\nFood of Angels, have mercy on us.\nHidden Manna, have mercy on us.\nMemorial of the wonders of God, have mercy on us.\nSupersubstantial Bread, have mercy on us.\nWord made flesh, dwelling among us, have mercy on us.\nHoly Host, have mercy on us.\nChalice of blessing, have mercy on us.\nMystery of faith, have mercy on us.\nSublime and venerable Sacrament, have mercy on us.\nMost holy of all Sacrifices, have mercy on us.\nTrue Propitiation for the living and the dead, have mercy on us.\nHeavenly medicine against all evils, have mercy on us.\nMiracle of miracles, have mercy on us.\nSacred memorial of the Lord's Passion, have mercy on us.\nPledge of future glory, have mercy on us.\n\nBe merciful, spare us, O Lord.\nBe merciful, graciously hear us, O Lord.\n\nFrom an unworthy reception of Your Body and Blood, deliver us, O Lord.\nFrom the lust of the flesh, deliver us, O Lord.\nFrom the pride of life, deliver us, O Lord.\nFrom every occasion of sin, deliver us, O Lord.\nThrough Your ardent desire to eat this Passover with Your disciples, deliver us, O Lord.\nThrough Your infinite love in instituting this Sacrament, deliver us, O Lord.\n\nWe sinners, beseech You, hear us.\nThat You would preserve and increase in us faith, reverence, and devotion toward this admirable Sacrament, we beseech You, hear us.\nThat You would conduct us to frequent reception of the Eucharist with pure hearts, we beseech You, hear us.\nThat You would preserve us from all heresy, sacrilege, and lukewarmness, we beseech You, hear us.\n\nLamb of God, who take away the sins of the world, spare us, O Lord.\nLamb of God, who take away the sins of the world, graciously hear us, O Lord.\nLamb of God, who take away the sins of the world, have mercy on us.\n\nV. You gave them bread from heaven.\nR. Containing in itself all sweetness.\n\nLet us pray: O God, who in this wonderful Sacrament left us a memorial of Your Passion: grant us, we implore You, so to venerate the sacred mysteries of Your Body and Blood, that we may ever perceive within ourselves the fruit of Your Redemption. Who lives and reigns world without end. Amen.",
  "prayerLitanyBlessedSacramentContentLatin": "Kyrie, eleison.\nChriste, eleison.\nKyrie, eleison.\n\nChriste, audi nos.\nChriste, exaudi nos.\n\nPater de caelis, Deus, miserere nobis.\nFili, Redemptor mundi, Deus, miserere nobis.\nSpiritus Sancte, Deus, miserere nobis.\nSancta Trinitas, unus Deus, miserere nobis.\n\nPanis vivus, qui de caelo descendisti, miserere nobis.\nDeus absconditus et Salvator, miserere nobis.\nFrumentum electorum, miserere nobis.\nVinum germinans virgines, miserere nobis.\nPanis pinguis et daps regalis, miserere nobis.\nIuge sacrificium, miserere nobis.\nOblatio munda, miserere nobis.\nAgnus absque macula, miserere nobis.\nMensa purissima, miserere nobis.\nAngelorum esca, miserere nobis.\nManna absconditum, miserere nobis.\nMemoriale mirabilium Dei, miserere nobis.\nPanis supersubstantialis, miserere nobis.\nVerbum caro factum, habitans in nobis, miserere nobis.\nHostia sancta, miserere nobis.\nCalix benedictionis, miserere nobis.\nMysterium fidei, miserere nobis.\nPraecelsum et venerabile Sacramentum, miserere nobis.\nSacrificium omnium sanctissimum, miserere nobis.\nVere propitiatorium pro vivis et defunctis, miserere nobis.\nCaeleste antidotum, quo a peccatis praeservamur, miserere nobis.\nMiraculum praestantissimum, miserere nobis.\nMemoria sacratissima Passionis Dominicae, miserere nobis.\nPignus futurae gloriae, miserere nobis.\n\nPropitius esto, parce nobis, Domine.\nPropitius esto, exaudi nos, Domine.\n\nAb indigna Corporis et Sanguinis tui sumptione, libera nos, Domine.\nA concupiscentia carnis, libera nos, Domine.\nA superbia vitae, libera nos, Domine.\nAb omni peccandi occasione, libera nos, Domine.\nPer desiderium quo hoc Pascha cum discipulis manducare cupiisti, libera nos, Domine.\nPer immensam caritatem qua hoc Sacramentum instituisti, libera nos, Domine.\n\nPeccatores, te rogamus, audi nos.\nUt fidem, reverentiam et devotionem erga hoc admirabile Sacramentum in nobis augere digneris, te rogamus, audi nos.\nUt ad frequentem et dignam sanctae Eucharistiae sumptionem nos perducere digneris, te rogamus, audi nos.\nUt ab omni haeresi, sacrilegio et cordis tepore nos praeservare digneris, te rogamus, audi nos.\n\nAgnus Dei, qui tollis peccata mundi, parce nobis, Domine.\nAgnus Dei, qui tollis peccata mundi, exaudi nos, Domine.\nAgnus Dei, qui tollis peccata mundi, miserere nobis.\n\nV. Panem de caelo praestitisti eis.\nR. Omne delectamentum in se habentem.\n\nOremus: Deus, qui nobis sub sacramento mirabili passionis tuae memoriam reliquisti: tribue, quaesumus, ita nos Corporis et Sanguinis tui sacra mysteria venerari, ut redemptionis tuae fructum in nobis iugiter sentiamus. Qui vivis et regnas in saecula saeculorum. Amen.",
  "prayerLitanyHolyAngelsTitle": "Litany of the Holy Angels",
  "prayerLitanyHolyAngelsContent": "Lord, have mercy on us.\nChrist, have mercy on us.\nLord, have mercy on us.\n\nChrist, hear us.\nChrist, graciously hear us.\n\nGod the Father of Heaven, have mercy on us.\nGod the Son, Redeemer of the world, have mercy on us.\nGod the Holy Spirit, have mercy on us.\nHoly Trinity, One God, have mercy on us.\n\nHoly Mary, Queen of Angels, pray for us.\nSaint Michael the Archangel, pray for us.\nSaint Gabriel the Archangel, pray for us.\nSaint Raphael the Archangel, pray for us.\nHoly Angels and Archangels, pray for us.\nHoly Seraphim, Cherubim, and Thrones, pray for us.\nHoly Dominions, Powers, and Virtues, pray for us.\nHoly Principalities, pray for us.\nHoly Guardian Angels, pray for us.\nHoly Angels, our defenders in spiritual combat, pray for us.\nHoly Angels, messengers of the Divine Will, pray for us.\nHoly Angels, who constantly behold the face of the Father in Heaven, pray for us.\nHoly Angels, our comforters in tribulation, pray for us.\nHoly Angels, our companions on our pilgrimage, pray for us.\nHoly Angels, our strength in time of temptation, pray for us.\nHoly Angels, who present our prayers to God, pray for us.\nHoly Angels, our comfort in the agony of death, pray for us.\nHoly Angels, who conduct the souls of the just to Paradise, pray for us.\n\nLamb of God, who take away the sins of the world, spare us, O Lord.\nLamb of God, who take away the sins of the world, graciously hear us, O Lord.\nLamb of God, who take away the sins of the world, have mercy on us.\n\nV. He has given His Angels charge over you.\nR. To keep you in all your ways.\n\nLet us pray: O God, who in Your unfathomable providence send Your holy Angels to watch over us, grant that we, Your suppliants, may always be defended by their protection on earth and share in their eternal fellowship in Heaven. Through Christ our Lord. Amen.",
  "prayerLitanyHolyAngelsContentLatin": "Kyrie, eleison.\nChriste, eleison.\nKyrie, eleison.\n\nChriste, audi nos.\nChriste, exaudi nos.\n\nPater de caelis, Deus, miserere nobis.\nFili, Redemptor mundi, Deus, miserere nobis.\nSpiritus Sancte, Deus, miserere nobis.\nSancta Trinitas, unus Deus, miserere nobis.\n\nSancta Maria, Regina Angelorum, ora pro nobis.\nSancte Michael Archangele, ora pro nobis.\nSancte Gabriel Archangele, ora pro nobis.\nSancte Raphael Archangele, ora pro nobis.\nSancti Angeli et Archangeli, orate pro nobis.\nSancti Seraphim, Cherubim et Throni, orate pro nobis.\nSanctae Dominationes, Potestates et Virtutes, orate pro nobis.\nSancti Principatus, orate pro nobis.\nSancti Angeli Custodes nostri, orate pro nobis.\nSancti Angeli, defensores nostri in certamine spiritali, orate pro nobis.\nSancti Angeli, nuntii divinae voluntatis, orate pro nobis.\nSancti Angeli, qui faciem Patris assidue contemplamini, orate pro nobis.\nSancti Angeli, consolatores in afflictionibus, orate pro nobis.\nSancti Angeli, fideles comites peregrinationis nostrae, orate pro nobis.\nSancti Angeli, robur nostrum in tempore tentationis, orate pro nobis.\nSancti Angeli, qui orationes nostras Deo offertis, orate pro nobis.\nSancti Angeli, solatores nostri in agone mortis, orate pro nobis.\nSancti Angeli, ductores animarum in Paradisum, orate pro nobis.\n\nAgnus Dei, qui tollis peccata mundi, parce nobis, Domine.\nAgnus Dei, qui tollis peccata mundi, exaudi nos, Domine.\nAgnus Dei, qui tollis peccata mundi, miserere nobis.\n\nV. Angelis suis Deus mandavit de te.\nR. Ut custodiant te in omnibus viis tuis.\n\nOremus: Deus, qui ineffabili providentia sanctos Angelos tuos ad nostram custodiam mittere dignaris: largire supplicibus tuis, et eorum semper protectione defendi, et aeterna societate gaudere. Per Christum Dominum nostrum. Amen.",
  "prayerLitanyGoodDeathTitle": "Litany for a Good Death",
  "prayerLitanyGoodDeathContent": "Lord Jesus, God of goodness and Father of mercies, I approach You with a contrite and humble heart; to You I recommend my last hour and what awaits me after it.\n\nWhen my motionless feet remind me that my course in this world is almost run, merciful Jesus, have mercy on me.\nWhen my trembling hands can no longer hold the Crucifix and I let it fall upon my bed of pain, merciful Jesus, have mercy on me.\nWhen my eyes, dim and clouded by the approach of death, fix their last look upon You, merciful Jesus, have mercy on me.\nWhen my cold and trembling lips utter for the last time Your adorable Name, merciful Jesus, have mercy on me.\nWhen my ears, closed to human words, listen to Your divine and irrevocable sentence, merciful Jesus, have mercy on me.\nWhen my soul, troubled by the anguish of death, struggles against the assaults of the devil, merciful Jesus, have mercy on me.\nWhen my heart beats faintly and fights the last battles of agony, merciful Jesus, have mercy on me.\nWhen my soul departs from my body, leaving it pale, cold and lifeless, receive my spirit into Your hands, merciful Jesus, have mercy on me.\n\nLet us pray: O God, who has doomed us to die, but concealed from us the hour of our death: grant that, passing all our days in justice and holiness, we may be worthy to depart this life in Your holy love. Through Jesus Christ our Lord. Amen.",
  "prayerLitanyGoodDeathContentLatin": "Domine Iesu, Deus bonitatis et Pater misericordiarum, contrito et humiliato corde ad Te accedo; Tibi ultimam meam horam et quidquid me post eam manet commendo.\n\nCum pedes mei immobiles me commonefacient cursum meum in hoc saeculo finiri, misericors Iesu, miserere mei.\nCum manus meae trementes Crucifixum tenere non poterunt, misericors Iesu, miserere mei.\nCum oculi mei caligantes in Te ultimum aspectum figent, misericors Iesu, miserere mei.\nCum labia mea frigida et trementia ultimum nomen Tuum invocabunt, misericors Iesu, miserere mei.\nCum aures meae vocibus hominum clausae Te solum iudicem audient, misericors Iesu, miserere mei.\nCum anima mea in agone mortis contra insidias diaboli decertabit, misericors Iesu, miserere mei.\nCum cor meum languidum ultimos motus efficiet, misericors Iesu, miserere mei.\nCum anima mea e corpore evolabit, suscipe spiritum meum in manus tuas, misericors Iesu, miserere mei.\n\nOremus: Deus, qui nos mori statuisti, sed horam mortis nostrae occultasti: concede ut in iustitia et sanctitate omnes dies vitae nostrae transeuntes, in caritate tua ex hoc saeculo migrare mereamur. Per Christum Dominum nostrum. Amen.",
  "prayerConsecTotusTuusTitle": "Totus Tuus (consecration to Mary)",
  "prayerConsecTotusTuusContent": "Totus Tuus ego sum, et omnia mea tua sunt.\n\nI belong entirely to you, O Mary, and all that I have is yours. I take you this day, my Mother, for my all. Lend me your Heart that I may love God with the same purity and fervor with which you loved Him.\n\nReceive me, Immaculate Virgin, under your maternal protection. Guard my senses, purify my soul, and sanctify all my actions, that I may live solely for Jesus, through you and with you.\n\nTotus Tuus ego sum, et omnia mea tua sunt. Amen.",
  "prayerConsecTotusTuusContentLatin": "Totus Tuus ego sum, et omnia mea tua sunt.\n\nAccipio te in mea omnia, o Maria, Mater mea dulcissima. Praebe mihi cor tuum, ut Deum eodem amore et puritate qua tu amasti diligere valeam.\n\nSuscipe me, Virgo Immaculata, sub materno praesidio tuo. Custodi sensus meos, munda animam meam, et omnes actiones meas sanctifica, ut soli Iesu per te et tecum vivam.\n\nTotus Tuus ego sum, et omnia mea tua sunt. Amen.",
  "prayerConsecMontfortTitle": "Consecration to Jesus through Mary (Saint Louis de Montfort)",
  "prayerConsecMontfortContent": "O Eternal and Incarnate Wisdom! O sweetest and most adorable Jesus! True God and true man, only Son of the Eternal Father, and of Mary, always virgin! I adore You profoundly in the bosom and splendors of Your Father, during eternity; and I adore You also in the virginal bosom of Mary, Your most worthy Mother, in the time of Your Incarnation.\n\nI give You thanks that You have annihilated Yourself, taking the form of a slave in order to rescue me from the cruel slavery of the devil. I praise and glorify You that You have been pleased to submit Yourself to Mary, Your holy Mother, in all things, in order to make me Your faithful slave through her. But, alas! Ungrateful and unfaithful as I am, I have not kept the promises which I made so solemnly to You in my Baptism; I have not fulfilled my obligations; I do not deserve to be called Your child, nor even Your slave; and as there is nothing in me which does not merit Your anger and Your repulse, I dare no more come by myself before Your most holy and august Majesty.\n\nIt is on this account that I have recourse to the intercession and mercy of Your holy Mother, whom You have given me for a mediatrix with You. It is through her that I hope to obtain of You contrition, the pardon of my sins, and the acquisition and preservation of wisdom.\n\nHail, then, O Immaculate Mary, living tabernacle of the Divinity, where the Eternal Wisdom willed to be hidden and to be adored by angels and by men! Hail, O Queen of Heaven and earth, to whose empire everything is subject which is under God! Hail, O sure refuge of sinners, whose mercy fails no one! Hear the desires which I have of the divine Wisdom; and for that end receive the vows and offerings which in my lowliness I present to you.\n\nI, a faithless sinner, renew and ratify today in your hands the vows of my Baptism; I renounce forever Satan, his pomps and works; and I give myself entirely to Jesus Christ, the Incarnate Wisdom, to carry my cross after Him all the days of my life, and to be more faithful to Him than I have ever been before.\n\nIn the presence of all the heavenly court I choose you this day for my Mother and Mistress. I deliver and consecrate to you, as your slave, my body and soul, my goods, both interior and exterior, and even the value of all my good actions, past, present, and future; leaving to you the entire and full right of disposing of me, and all that belongs to me, without exception, according to your good pleasure, for the greater glory of God in time and in eternity.\n\nReceive, O benevolent Virgin, this little offering of my slavery, in honor of, and in union with, that subjection which the Eternal Wisdom deigned to have to your maternity; in homage to the power which both of you have over this poor sinner, and in thanksgiving for the privileges with which the Holy Trinity has favored you. I protest that I wish henceforth, as your true slave, to seek your honor and to obey you in all things.\n\nO admirable Mother, present me to your dear Son as His eternal slave, so that as He has redeemed me by you, by you He may receive me!\n\nO Mother of mercy, grant me the grace to obtain the true Wisdom of God; and for that end receive me among those whom you love and teach, whom you lead, nourish and protect as your children and your slaves.\n\nO faithful Virgin, make me in all things so perfect a disciple, imitator and slave of the Incarnate Wisdom, Jesus Christ your Son, that I may attain, by your intercession and by your example, to the fullness of His age on earth and of His glory in Heaven. Amen.",
  "prayerConsecMontfortContentLatin": "O Aeterna et Incarnata Sapientia! O dulcissime et adorabilis Iesu, verus Deus et verus homo, Fili unigenite Patris Aeterni et Mariae semper Virginis! Te profundissime adoro in sinu et splendoribus Patris tui in aeternitate, atque in sinu virginali Mariae, sanctissimae Matris tuae, in tempore Incarnationis tuae.\n\nGratias tibi ago quod teipsum exinanisti, formam servi accipiens, ut me a crudeli diaboli servitute liberares. Te laudo et glorifico quod Mariae, Matri tuae sanctissimae, in omnibus subditus esse voluisti, ut me per ipsam fidelem servum tuum efficeres. Sed heu! ingratus et infidelis, promissa meo Baptismate tam solemniter facta non servavi; ideo confugio ad misericordiam et intercessionem sanctissimae Matris tuae, quam mihi mediatricem dedisti.\n\nAve igitur, o Maria Immaculata, vivum Divinitatis tabernaculum! Ave, Regina caeli et terrae! Ave, refugium peccatorum! Ego infidelis peccator renovo et ratifico hodie in manibus tuis vota mei Baptismi: renuntio in perpetuum satanae, pompis et operibus eius, et me totum trado Iesu Christo, Sapientiae Incarnatae, ad crucem meam post eum ferendam omnibus diebus vitae meae.\n\nEligo te hodie, coram omni curia caelesti, in Matrem et Dominam meam. Trado et consecro tibi, in statu servi, corpus et animam meam, bona mea interiora et exteriora, atque ipsum pretium bonorum meorum actuum praeteritorum, praesentium et futurorum, relinquens tibi plenum et integrum ius de me disponendi secundum beneplacitum tuum, ad maiorem Dei gloriam in tempore et in aeternitate.\n\nAccipe, o Virgo benigna, hanc meae servitutis oblationem, et praesenta me dilecto Filio tuo tamquam servum sempiternum, ut qui me per te redemit, per te me recipiat. Amen.",
  "prayerConsecSacredHeartTitle": "Consecration to the Sacred Heart of Jesus",
  "prayerConsecSacredHeartContent": "I give and consecrate to the Sacred Heart of our Lord Jesus Christ my person and my life, my actions, pains, and sufferings, so that I may be unwilling to make use of any part of my being other than to honor, love, and glorify Him.\n\nThis is my unchanging purpose, namely, to be all His, and to do all things for the love of Him, at the same time renouncing with all my heart whatever is displeasing to Him.\n\nI therefore take You, O Sacred Heart, to be the only object of my love, the guardian of my life, the assurance of my salvation, the remedy of my weakness and inconstancy, the atonement for all the faults of my life, and my sure refuge at the hour of death.\n\nBe, then, O Heart of goodness, my justification before God Your Father, and turn away from me the strokes of His righteous anger. O Heart of love, I put all my trust in You, for I fear everything from my own weakness, but I hope for all things from Your goodness and mercy.\n\nRemove from me all that can displease You or resist Your holy will; let Your pure love imprint Your image so deeply upon my heart, that I shall never be able to forget You or to be separated from You.\n\nMay I obtain from all Your loving-kindness the grace of having my name written in Your Heart, for in You I desire to place all my happiness and all my glory, living and dying in Your holy service.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerConsecSacredHeartContentLatin": "Ego me totum trado et consecro Sacratissimo Cordi Domini nostri Iesu Christi: personam et vitam meam, actiones, aerumnas et dolores meos, ut nulla amplius entis mei parte uti velim, nisi ad Ipsum honorandum, amandum et glorificandum.\n\nHaec est voluntas mea irrevocabilis: totum Eius esse, et omnia pro Eius amore facere, renuntiando ex toto corde meo omnibus quae Ipsi displicere possunt.\n\nTe igitur eligo, o Cor Sacratissimum, in unicum meae dilectionis obiectum, vitae meae custodem, salutis meae securitatem, meae infirmitatis et inconstantiae remedium, omnium vitae meae culparum expiationem, atque certum in hora mortis refugium.\n\nEsto igitur, o Cor bonitatis, mea iustificatio apud Deum Patrem tuum, et averte a me iustae Ipsius irae flagella. O Cor dilectionis, in Te totam fiduciam meam pono; omnia enim timeo a mea fragilitate, sed omnia spero a tua bonitate!\n\nDele in me quidquid Tibi displicere vel resistere potest; infige amorem tuum tam alte cordi meo, ut numquam Tui oblivisci neque a Te separari valeam.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerConsecStJosephTitle": "Consecration to Saint Joseph",
  "prayerConsecStJosephContent": "To you, O blessed Joseph, do we fly in our tribulation, and having implored the help of your most holy Spouse, we now, with hearts full of confidence, earnestly crave your safeguard also.\n\nBy that bond of sacred charity which united you to the Immaculate Virgin Mother of God, and by that fatherly love with which you embraced the Child Jesus, we humbly beg you to look graciously upon the beloved inheritance which Jesus Christ purchased by His divine Blood, and by your power and strength to aid us in our necessities.\n\nDefend, O most watchful guardian of the Holy Family, the chosen offspring of Jesus Christ. Keep from us, O most loving father, all blight of error and corrupting influence. Aid us from on high, most valiant defender, in this conflict with the powers of darkness.\n\nAnd even as of old you rescued the Child Jesus from the peril of His life, so now defend God's Holy Church from the snares of the enemy and from all adversity. Shield us ever under your patronage, that, following your example and strengthened by your help, we may live a holy life, die a happy death, and attain to everlasting bliss in Heaven.\n\nAmen.",
  "prayerConsecStJosephContentLatin": "Ad te, beate Ioseph, in tribulatione nostra confugimus, atque, implorato Sponsae tuae sanctissimae auxilio, patrocinium quoque tuum fidenter exposcimus.\n\nPer eam, quaesumus, quae te cum immaculata Virgine Dei Genetrice coniunxit, caritatis necessitudinem, perque paternum, quo Puerum Iesum amplexus es, amorem, supplices deprecamur, ut ad hereditatem, quam Iesus Christus acquisivit Sanguine suo, benignus respicias, ac necessitatibus nostris tua virtute et ope succurras.\n\nTuere, o Custos providentissime divinae Familiae, Iesu Christi sobolem electam; prohibe a nobis, amantissime pater, omnem errorum ac corruptelarum luem; propitius nobis, sospitator noster fortissime, in hoc cum potestate tenebrarum certamine e caelo adesto.\n\nEt sicut olim Puerum Iesum e summo eripuisti vitae discrimine, ita nunc sanctam Dei Ecclesiam ab hostilibus insidiis atque omni adversitate defende: nosque singulos perpetuo tege patrocinio, ut ad tui exemplar et ope suffulti, sancte vivere, pie emori, sempiternamque in caelis beatitudinem assequi valeamus.\n\nAmen.",
